        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_292_15.jpg",
        "description": "Adding volume at the crown can make Old Hollywood side-swept curls feel even more glamorous and can help balance strong facial features. This hairstyle combines a deep side part, a bit of lift at the crown, and flowing curls directed over one shoulder.\n\nAfter washing, apply a volumizing mousse to the roots and blow-dry using a round brush, lifting hair up and away from the scalp in the crown area. You can backcomb lightly underneath the top layers at the crown for extra height, then smooth the surface with a comb so it looks polished, not messy. Curl the rest of the hair in the same direction around the head and allow it to cool. Brush into waves and sweep everything over to the heavier side of the part, making sure the slight lift at the crown transitions smoothly into the side-swept curls. Finish with a firm-hold hairspray focused at the crown and around the front hairline to keep the volume intact throughout the night.",
