        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_292_4.jpg",
        "description": "A deep side part is almost non-negotiable when you want the most dramatic Old Hollywood side-swept curls, because it creates instant asymmetry and contour around the face. This hairstyle emphasizes the part even more by smoothing the smaller side close to the scalp while allowing the heavier side to showcase those sculpted curls.\n\nStart by drawing your part well past the arch of your brow, then use a fine-tooth comb and a light gel or styling cream to keep the smaller side neat and controlled. Curl the heavier side in medium sections, all in the same direction, and clip each curl to cool so they hold a uniform shape.\n\nWhen you brush everything out, guide the waves to frame your cheekbone and jawline as they sweep down, creating that camera-ready profile. Set the smooth side with hairspray and, if needed, bobby pins hidden under the top layer, so the focus remains on the glossy, defined curls on the other side.",
