        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_292_11.jpg",
        "description": "For the most authentic Old Hollywood side-swept curls, a pin curl set delivers that true vintage structure and long-lasting hold. This hairstyle uses wet or damp hair formed into curls, pinned flat against the head, and allowed to dry completely before brushing out.\n\nStart with slightly damp hair and a setting lotion, then create small sections, wrapping them around your finger into spiral shapes and pinning them flat to your scalp in the direction you want your waves to flow. Focus on creating a deep side part and making sure the curls on the heavier side all roll in the same direction. Once hair is fully dry, remove the pins and brush the curls into soft waves, guiding them over one shoulder and smoothing the smaller side back. This method produces that classic, sculpted wave pattern that can last all evening, especially when finished with a mist of strong-hold hairspray for a truly retro, photo-ready finish.",
