        "description": "Adding a hair accessory can instantly personalize Old Hollywood side-swept curls and tie your hairstyle into your outfit or event theme. This look still centers on a deep side part and flowing curls over one shoulder, but features a decorative accessory placed strategically at the part or above the ear on the tucked side.\n\nThink of a jeweled clip, pearl barrette, or delicate comb, which can echo vintage glamour without overpowering the hairstyle. After curling and brushing your hair into smooth waves, tuck the smaller side behind your ear and secure it with bobby pins.\n\nThen place your accessory over the pinned section so it hides the hardware while drawing the eye to the smooth curve of the curls on the opposite side. Keep accessories lightweight so they do not drag down the hair, and finish with a light mist of hairspray to hold everything in place without dulling the sparkle of the accessory.",
