        "description": "Short hair can absolutely rock Old Hollywood side-swept curls, and the result is often incredibly chic and fashion-forward. This version works well on chin-length bobs or slightly longer cuts, using structured waves to create a sleek, sculpted shape that hugs the jawline.\n\nStart by creating a deep side part and blow-drying hair smooth with a round brush for a polished base. Then use a smaller barrel curling iron or even flat iron waves, curling all sections in the same direction so they later form a continuous pattern.\n\nAfter cooling, brush out the curls gently to create defined S-waves rather than tight ringlets, and tuck the shorter side behind the ear to emphasize the side sweep. Finish with a strong-hold hairspray and a touch of shine serum, which helps the waves look glossy and deliberate while keeping the overall style compact and neat.",
