        "numberTitle": "4. Braided Pigtail Curls For Girls",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_294_6.jpg",
        "description": "Braided pigtail curls mix the neatness of braids with the playful bounce of curly ends, making them a favorite for picture days and events. Part the hair into two sections, then create a three-strand braid, French braid, or Dutch braid on each side from the scalp down toward the shoulders.\n\nStop braiding a few inches from the ends and secure each braid with a small elastic so you have loose hair left at the bottom. Apply curl cream or mousse to these loose ends and scrunch to shape the curls, or set them in heatless rollers if the hair is naturally straight.\n\nThe braids keep the roots and mid-lengths smooth, while the ends form soft coils that add movement and volume. This combination is practical for active kids because it reduces tangles yet still looks soft and feminine.",
