        "numberTitle": "15. Dutch Braided Pigtail Curls For Girls",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_294_7.jpg",
        "description": "Dutch braided pigtail curls sit slightly raised from the scalp, adding texture and structure before flowing into loose curls. Create a middle part, then start a\n\nDutch braid on each side, crossing the strands under instead of over so the braid stands out. Continue braiding along the head shape until you reach the nape, then secure with an elastic to form two low pigtails. Leave the remaining lengths loose and enhance them with curl cream, twisting small pieces around your finger to define each curl. If your child\u2019s hair is straight, you can braid the loose sections overnight or use soft flexi rods to create smooth spirals by morning. This hairstyle holds up well for long days and works beautifully for school, sports, and even family photos since it looks polished from every angle.",
