        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_294_12.jpg",
        "description": "Sectioned pigtail curls use small elastics to create a ladder of mini ponytails that lead into curled ends. Begin by parting the hair into two main sides, then divide each side into several horizontal sections from the top of the head down to the nape.\n\nOn each side, secure the top section into a mini ponytail, then combine it with the next section below using another elastic, working your way downward. At the bottom, you\u2019ll have two larger pigtails made from all the connected sections, which creates a visually interesting pattern.\n\nCurl the loose lengths of these final pigtails with heatless techniques or a curling wand on low heat to form smooth spirals. This style keeps hair neatly controlled and is especially helpful for longer or thicker hair that tangles easily during the day.",
