        "numberTitle": "18. French Braided Pigtail Curls For Girls",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_294_8.jpg",
        "description": "French braided pigtail curls are a classic choice that keeps hair off the face while showcasing soft curls at the ends. Start with a middle part and gather a small triangle of hair near the forehead on one side, then begin a\n\nFrench braid by adding hair as you move toward the back. Once you reach the nape, secure the braid with an elastic to create a pigtail, leaving the rest of the hair loose. Repeat on the other side, trying to keep the tension even so both braids sit at the same height and feel comfortable. Apply curl-defining cream through the loose lengths and gently scrunch, or set them in soft rollers for heatless curls if needed.\n\nThis look is great for school or special events because the braids control flyaways while the curly ends keep the hairstyle light and playful.",
