        "numberTitle": "1. Curly Ends With Straight Roots For Picture Day",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_295_13.jpg",
        "description": "If your child prefers a neater top but still wants curls on the ends, a look with straight roots and curly ends is a nice compromise for school picture day. Blow dry or stretch just the roots and mid-lengths with a brush while leaving the bottom parts slightly damp.\n\nThen use a curling wand or small rollers on the lower sections to create smooth, consistent curls. This method keeps the scalp area flatter and easier to control, which can help with cowlicks or uneven parts. Once curls are set and cooled, lightly finger comb them so they look soft and natural. Finish with a small amount of serum or light oil on the ends for shine.\n\nIn photos, the top looks tidy while the curled ends add movement and interest.",
