        "numberTitle": "2. Half Up School Picture Day Curls",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_295_2.jpg",
        "description": "For kids who like hair out of their face but still want to show off curls, a half up curly look is a great school picture day option. This style keeps the hairline and bangs controlled so the focus stays on their eyes and smile in the photo.\n\nStart by defining curls with a curl cream or lightweight mousse on damp hair, then either air-dry or diffuse. Once the curls are set, gather the top section from temples back to the crown and secure it with a small elastic, barrette, or clip. Keep the tension gentle so you do not flatten the curls at the roots. Let the lower section of hair fall freely in soft curls over the shoulders.\n\nThis gives a sweet, polished finish that still feels playful and kid-friendly.",
