        "numberTitle": "3. Curly High Puff For Picture Day",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_295_6.jpg",
        "description": "A curly high puff is a cute and practical school picture day option, especially for kids with tight coils or highly textured curls. This look brings all the curls up toward the crown of the head, creating a full, fluffy shape that photographs beautifully from the front.\n\nStart with moisturized hair, applying leave-in conditioner and a light gel or cream around the edges for smoothness. Use a soft brush to gently gather the hair upward and secure it with a puff cuff, stretched headband, or loose tie that will not cause breakage. Keep the edges smooth but not overly sleek so the style still looks soft and youthful. Fluff the puff with your fingers to create an even, rounded shape of curls.\n\nThis style keeps hair off the neck and face, while still letting the curl pattern be the star of the picture.",
