        "description": "A curly ponytail keeps hair tidy and out of the way while still letting curls shine for school picture day. This is perfect for kids who dislike hair on their neck or in their eyes but still want a fun, bouncy look in photos.\n\nStart by defining curls with a styling cream or mousse, letting them dry fully before gathering them up. Decide between a mid-height pony at the back of the head or a slightly higher pony for more visible volume. Use your fingers, not a fine comb, to bring the hair back so you keep the natural curl texture and avoid frizz. Secure with a soft, snag-free elastic and wrap a small piece of hair around the base if you want a more polished finish.\n\nLeave a few face-framing curls out in front to soften the look on camera.",
