        "numberTitle": "13. Curly Crown Braid With Curls",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_295_12.jpg",
        "description": "A curly crown braid with the rest of the hair left loose in curls gives a sweet, picture-perfect look for school photos. This style frames the face with both braids and curls, adding interest without being overly complicated.\n\nStart by parting the hair slightly off-center and taking a small section from one side near the hairline. Braid this section along the front, moving toward the opposite side and securing with a small clear elastic or pin. Repeat on the other side if you want a full crown effect, or keep just one braid for a simpler version. Define the remaining hair with curl cream and let it dry into soft curls around the shoulders.\n\nThe braid helps keep hair out of the eyes while the loose curls add volume and texture in the photo.",
