        "numberTitle": "4. Curled Under Bob For Thick Hair",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_298_13.jpg",
        "description": "On thick hair, a curled under bob looks glossy and luxurious when the cut is tailored to remove bulk without sacrificing shape. Stylists often use internal layering, undercutting, or slide cutting to thin out the interior while leaving the perimeter strong so the ends still read as a bob when curled under.\n\nThis keeps the silhouette smooth and controlled rather than puffy or triangular. When styling, work in smaller sections and use a medium or large round brush to smooth the cuticle and bend the ends, keeping tension consistent so the curl under looks sleek instead of bouncy.\n\nA smoothing cream or light oil from midlengths to ends, plus an anti humidity spray, helps manage frizz and keep the shape intact even in warmer weather.",
