        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_298_7.jpg",
        "description": "Pairing a curled under bob with curtain bangs is an easy way to soften your features and make the cut feel more romantic. The bob itself can sit anywhere from the jaw to the shoulders, but the key is longer bangs that split down the middle and sweep off to each side, blending into the rest of the cut.\n\nWhen both the fringe and the hem are curled under, you get a face-framing effect that highlights the eyes and cheekbones without feeling heavy. To style, blow-dry the bangs first with a small round brush, rolling them back and then down so they naturally separate, then use a medium brush or flat iron to tuck the bob\u2019s ends under. A light texturizing spray at the roots keeps the fringe from separating into flat pieces and adds lift so the overall look stays airy., Fresh Look",
