        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_301_1.jpg",
        "description": "On lazy mornings, a refreshed wash and go is often the easiest way to bring curls back to life without redoing every step from wash day. Lightly mist your hair with water or a curl-refresh spray until it feels slightly damp, then scrunch to reactivate your existing gel or cream for renewed definition.\n\nFocus extra moisture and product on the outer layer and hairline where frizz and flattening usually show first. If certain sections look stretched, finger coil a few curls around your finger to tighten the pattern again.\n\nLet your hair air-dry or do a quick diffuse to lock in volume, keeping your hands off while it sets to avoid frizz. This simple refresh keeps your original shape, boosts shine, and makes your curls look newly styled with minimal effort.",
