        "numberTitle": "13. Curly Claw Clip Refresh Updo",
        "image": "assets/curly_hairstyles_301_5.jpg",
        "description": "When your curls look good at the ends but frizz has taken over the mid-lengths and roots, a claw clip refresh updo is a fast fix. Lightly mist the upper layers with water, then smooth a bit of styling cream or gel over the outer surface, focusing on halo frizz.\n\nGather your curls at the back of your head as if making a low ponytail, twist once or twice, then flip the twist up and secure it with a large claw clip. Let some curls spill over the top of the clip for a soft, undone shape.\n\nPull out a few tendrils at the front and around your ears, then finger coil any stretched pieces with a little extra product. This refreshed updo looks intentional and chic while hiding messy sections and extending your wash day for another one or two outings.",
