        "description": "Look closely at the beautiful architecture of a truly well-cut bob. The curly graduated bob is a masterclass in precision and shape.\n\nThe hair at the nape is cut the shortest, and it gradually gets longer as it moves up toward the temples. When curly hair is cut this way, it forms a perfect outward curve. The curls stack on top of each other like shingles on a roof. This creates incredible density at the back of the head. It is a very polished and put-together look. This cut requires regular trims every six weeks to maintain the sharp graduated shape.\n\nIt is worth the effort for such a flawless finish.",
