        "description": "Embracing your gray can feel empowering, especially when the cut shows off the natural dimension and texture. A modern wavy shag for gray hair uses layered sections to highlight the different tones in silver, white, and salt-and-pepper strands.\n\nThe choppy layers help break up any solid areas so hair looks more textured and lively rather than flat. Ask for a soft, face-framing fringe and medium layering through the crown to give lift where gray hair sometimes collapses.\n\nStyling is simple: apply a curl cream or light mousse, scrunch, and let air-dry, then finish with a shine spray to enhance the natural sheen of gray. This look feels chic and current, showing that gray hair can be a statement feature when paired with a thoughtfully cut, modern shag shape that flatters your features.",
