        "description": "A chin-length cut can feel refreshing when you want a noticeable change without going extremely short. A chin length wavy shag bob has a bob-like outline that lands around the jawline, while layered sections throughout add lift and texture.\n\nThis combination keeps the style from looking too boxy or severe, which is important when working with mature features. Ask your stylist to keep the back slightly shorter and the front gently longer, creating a soft angle that frames the face and visually lengthens the neck. Light point-cutting at the ends prevents the cut from feeling blunt while enhancing your natural waves. For daily styling, rough-dry with your fingers or a diffuser, then pinch a bit of texturizing cream into the ends for separation and that modern, undone finish.\n\nThis bob works particularly well if you like showing off necklines and earrings.",
