        "numberTitle": "13. Short Wavy Shag For Fine Hair Over 50",
        "image": "assets/curly_over50_281_1.jpg",
        "description": "Light, airy texture is the secret to making fine hair look fuller without a lot of effort in your daily routine. A short wavy shag for women over 50 keeps length around the ears and nape but uses choppy layers through the crown to create instant lift.\n\nThis shape prevents hair from collapsing flat against the scalp and instead builds a soft, rounded silhouette that feels modern and youthful. Ask your stylist for razor or point-cut layers, focusing on removing bulk at the top and keeping slightly longer pieces around the temples to gently frame the face.\n\nStyling is simple: apply a lightweight volumizing mousse at the roots, scrunch in a wave-enhancing cream, then either air-dry or diffuse for extra bounce. A soft, side-swept fringe can help hide forehead lines while blending seamlessly into the rest of the cut so it never feels harsh or heavy.",
