        "numberTitle": "14. Wavy Shag Haircut For Thin Hair Over 50",
        "image": "assets/curly_over50_281_18.jpg",
        "description": "When hair becomes thinner with age, the right cut can create the illusion of much more fullness. A wavy shag haircut for thin hair over 50 focuses on adding volume at the crown and movement throughout, without overly thinning the ends.\n\nThe layers are placed carefully so they lift the hair away from the scalp and encourage a natural wave, which makes strands appear denser. Ask your stylist to keep the perimeter slightly blunt for strength while texturizing inside the cut for lift and softness.\n\nStyling products matter: a lightweight volumizing mousse or foam at the roots paired with a gentle wave spray on the lengths works best. Air-drying or using a diffuser on low heat can help preserve the volume you have, resulting in a fuller-looking, youthful shape that still feels very low effort day to day.",
