        "numberTitle": "15. Salt And Pepper Medium Wavy Shag Over 50",
        "image": "assets/curly_over50_281_9.jpg",
        "description": "Natural salt-and-pepper hair already has built-in contrast, and a well-cut shag can make that contrast look intentional and stylish. A medium wavy shag at shoulder length lets the grays and darker strands intermix through layered sections, creating depth without needing extra color services.\n\nThe layers add movement and prevent the hair from appearing blocky, which can sometimes happen with medium lengths. Ask for soft, rounded layers that focus on lifting the crown and lightly contouring the face, which can help highlight your cheekbones and eyes.\n\nStyling works best with a light texturizing spray or salt mist scrunched into damp hair, then either air-dried or diffused to encourage waves. This haircut is ideal if you like an effortless, slightly undone look that still feels put together and emphasizes the beauty of your natural salt-and-pepper shade.",
