        "numberTitle": "16. Wavy Shag Haircut With Feathered Layers Over 50",
        "image": "assets/curly_over50_281_17.jpg",
        "description": "Feathered layers are a classic choice that still feels relevant when combined with a modern shag shape. A wavy shag haircut with feathered layers over 50 uses soft, tapering ends that fan out, giving hair a light, airy quality.\n\nThe layering usually starts around the cheekbones or lower and continues through the ends, creating movement without sacrificing too much density. Ask for the layers to be cut with a razor or point-cutting technique to achieve that feathery, blended effect instead of harsh lines.\n\nWhen styling, a light mousse or volumizing spray at the roots combined with a wave cream on the mid-lengths can bring out the texture without weigh-down. This cut flatters many face shapes and works especially well if your hair is straight to wavy and you want a soft, swinging finish that feels timeless yet current.",
