        "numberTitle": "17. Shoulder Length Wavy Shag With Layers",
        "image": "assets/curly_over50_281_10.jpg",
        "description": "When you want a cut that feels versatile but not too long, shoulder length is a comfortable and flattering option. A shoulder length wavy shag uses layers starting around the lips or cheekbones, cascading down through the mid-lengths to create movement and prevent heaviness.\n\nThis structure keeps the perimeter looking soft instead of blunt, which often suits mature features better. Ask your stylist to keep the ends slightly textured and to build a bit of extra volume at the crown, which helps lift the overall shape.\n\nFor styling, a wave foam or curl cream scrunched into damp hair works nicely, and you can twist a few front pieces around a curling iron for extra definition if desired. This length is also easy to tie back for exercise or errands while still looking stylish and full when worn down with your natural waves.",
