        "numberTitle": "18. Wavy Shag Haircut For Thick Hair Over 50",
        "image": "assets/curly_over50_281_11.jpg",
        "description": "Thick hair can feel heavy and bulky, especially as you get older and prefer softer, more manageable styles. A wavy shag haircut for thick hair over 50 focuses on strategic layering to remove weight while keeping enough fullness for a healthy, voluminous look.\n\nThe layers are usually more pronounced, with internal texturizing that reduces bulk and encourages your natural wave pattern to show. Ask for a length that hits between the chin and shoulders, depending on your face shape, and request feathered ends so the hair flicks out softly rather than forming a solid block. Styling is easiest with a smoothing cream at the mid-lengths and a texturizing spray at the ends to keep everything light, separated, and bouncy. This kind of shag makes thick hair feel breathable and modern, with plenty of movement but far less daily effort than a one-length cut.",
