        "numberTitle": "2. Stacked Cheekbone Bob",
        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_250_15.jpg",
        "description": "The stacked cheekbone bob uses close-set, angled layers at the back of the head to build serious volume and structure. Unlike a simple layered bob, the stacking technique creates a rounded, voluminous shape at the crown and nape that contrasts with the flat, sleek cheekbone-length front pieces.\n\nIt\u2019s a very architectural cut that looks dimensional from every angle, including the back \u2014 which is often overlooked in bob variations. This style is a powerhouse for women with fine or limp hair because the stacked volume makes thin strands look dramatically fuller. It also adds height at the crown, which elongates the face proportions in a flattering way. Ask your stylist for a steep graduation in the back with a clean, sharp perimeter for the most polished stacked result.",
