        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_250_4.jpg",
        "description": "When you want your bob to feel edgy and modern rather than polished, the textured choppy cheekbone bob delivers every time. This version uses point-cutting or razor techniques to create uneven, piece-y ends that give the bob a raw, undone aesthetic.\n\nThe choppy texture adds serious dimension and personality, making even simple styling look intentional. It works beautifully on thick or medium hair, where the weight would otherwise flatten a blunt cut.\n\nThe length at the cheekbone means all that texture gets framed right around the face, making the style feel dynamic and fresh rather than messy. A small amount of texturizing paste worked through the ends is all you need to define the pieces and maximize that choppy, lived-in finish.",
