        "description": "The A-line cheekbone bob is a refined angled cut where the front pieces are noticeably longer than the back, creating that signature diagonal shape. When the front length stops right at the cheekbones, the whole look becomes dramatically face-framing and structured.\n\nThe contrast between the shorter back and the longer, cheek-grazing front creates visual interest from every angle. This is a brilliant cut for square or heart-shaped faces because the angle softens hard jawlines and draws focus to the mid-face instead.\n\nIt also photographs incredibly well because the diagonal line creates movement and depth. Ask your stylist for a crisp A-line with a moderate angle \u2014 too steep, and it starts to look asymmetrical; too subtle, and the effect is lost entirely.",
