        "description": "Thick hair and cheekbone-length bobs are actually an ideal match when the cut is done correctly. The key is removing interior bulk through strategic layering without disrupting the outer shape of the bob.\n\nA well-executed cheekbone bob on thick hair sits clean and structured without puffing out or weighing down. The length at the cheekbones works in your favor here \u2014 it\u2019s short enough that the weight doesn\u2019t pull the shape down, yet long enough to maintain a smooth, polished outline.\n\nAdding subtle internal layers and point-cut ends keeps the thickness manageable without creating a wispy or shapeless look. Women with thick hair should also ask for a light thinning of the ends to keep the perimeter sharp and the overall silhouette beautifully controlled and intentional.",
