        "numberTitle": "13. Inverted Cheekbone Bob",
        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_250_5.jpg",
        "description": "The inverted cheekbone bob \u2014 also called a graduated bob \u2014 is shorter at the back and gradually gets longer toward the front, ending right at cheekbone level. This angled structure creates a sleek, tapered silhouette at the nape while keeping length and face-framing volume at the front.\n\nThe stacked back adds incredible lift and body, making it a top pick for women with fine or flat hair who want noticeable volume without extensions or heavy products. The front pieces graze the cheekbones, framing the face perfectly and drawing the eye to your strongest features.\n\nIt\u2019s a style that looks clean and sharp from every angle. Blow dry the back layers upward and smooth the front pieces down for the most defined finish.",
