        "description": "Love the versatility of longer hair but crave that bouncy swing? A long bob with face framing layers, often called a lob, is the perfect compromise.\n\nThe length usually hits right at the collarbone, which naturally allows for more movement than a chin-length cut. The magic happens when your stylist adds face framing layers starting at the cheekbones. These layers cascade downward, creating a sweeping, diagonal flow that draws attention to your features. Because the interior is thinned out slightly, the hair swings freely instead of hanging heavily.\n\nYou can wear it straight for a sleek sway or add beachy waves to amplify the flowing texture. It remains one of the most universally flattering, highly dynamic options available today.",
