        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_256_11.jpg",
        "description": "Looking to bring back a little retro flair? The stacked bob with flipped ends takes a classic shape and injects it with a fun, lively bounce.\n\nThe stacking refers to the graduated, wedge-like layers at the back of the head that create built-in volume and lift. To push the movement factor over the top, the ends of the hair are flipped outward using a round brush or flat iron. This outward curve adds a springy, energetic finish that dances around your neck and face. The combination of the lifted, stacked back and the whimsical flipped front creates a push-and-pull dynamic. It is a fantastic choice for anyone wanting a cheerful, voluminous haircut that refuses to sit still.",
