        "numberTitle": "1. Inverted Undone Bob Haircut",
        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_259_12.jpg",
        "description": "An inverted undone bob haircut gives a subtle angle while still staying relaxed and unstructured. The back is cut slightly shorter and gradually lengthens toward the front, but instead of a rigid stacked look, the layers and edges are softened.\n\nStylists may use slicing or texturizing shears to break up the weight in the back, which allows the hair to curve naturally around the neck while the front pieces skim the collarbone or jaw. This shape works especially well for straight or wavy hair that needs a bit of built\u2011in movement and swing.\n\nTo style, blow\u2011dry brushing everything forward slightly to emphasize the angle, then add loose waves through the mid\u2011lengths only, finishing with a texture spray or dry wax so the inversion feels soft, not severe, and keeps that undone, breezy vibe.",
