        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_259_11.jpg",
        "description": "A shaggy undone bob haircut leans into rock\u2011inspired texture with lots of choppy layers and movement. It combines the best parts of a shag\u2014like piecey ends and crown volume\u2014with the structure of a bob length.\n\nHairdressers often use razors or deep point cutting to carve out texture, especially around the face and through the mid\u2011lengths, which gives that shattered effect without losing overall shape. This cut works nicely for medium to thick hair that can hold layers, and it pairs well with soft bangs or curtain fringe for extra attitude. Styling is fairly unfussy: apply a volumizing spray or mousse at the roots, scrunch in a wave spray through the lengths, then rough dry and finish with dry spray wax to highlight the shaggy pieces and keep everything looking intentionally messy.\u2019s Haircut Ideas for Wavy Medium Hair",
