        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_259_3.jpg",
        "description": "A cheekbone grazing undone bob feels playful and chic, especially if you love that slightly cropped, French\u2011inspired vibe. While it sits higher than a classic bob, the undone texture keeps it from feeling too drastic or boxy.\n\nThe length usually hovers between the middle of the cheek and the top of the jaw, with choppy, softened ends that gently trace the face contour. Many stylists pair this length with light, piecey face\u2011framing bits or a soft fringe, then add subtle layers through the crown so the hair does not collapse flat. Styling works best with minimal effort: apply a mousse or wave spray on damp hair, rough dry with fingers, then twist random sections around a small iron and shake them out for airy movement and separation.",
