        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_259_13.jpg",
        "description": "An asymmetrical undone bob haircut brings a little edge to the trend, with one side subtly longer than the other while the overall texture stays relaxed. The difference in length can be dramatic or minimal, depending on how bold you want the look to feel.\n\nStylists typically keep the shorter side slightly more tucked and controlled, while the longer side gets extra texture and movement to emphasize the imbalance in a flattering way. This kind of cut works well with natural waves, as the asymmetry naturally draws attention to cheekbones and jawline without needing a lot of styling effort.\n\nTo finish, use a heat protectant and tong a few random sections, then rake through with fingers and mist a flexible texture spray or wax, allowing some pieces to flip outward and others inward for a truly undone **feel**.",
