        "numberTitle": "5. Dark Brown With Caramel Face-Framing Bob Haircut",
        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_263_18.jpg",
        "description": "Combining a dark brown base with caramel face-framing pieces is a color technique that flatters almost everyone. This look keeps the overall hair color deep and rich while adding warmth and brightness around the face where it matters most.\n\nOn a bob haircut, those caramel highlights near the front help draw attention to your features and create a soft, flattering frame. The contrast between the dark base and the lighter front pieces adds visual interest and dimension without requiring a full highlights appointment. This color combination works on all skin tones and can be adjusted to be more subtle or more dramatic based on your preference. The dark base means root regrowth is barely noticeable, and the face-framing pieces can be refreshed during quick touch-up visits.\n\nFor a bob that feels polished, face-brightening, and naturally beautiful, this color pairing is a winner.",
