        "numberTitle": "12. Warm Blonde Highlights Bob Haircut",
        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_263_14.jpg",
        "description": "Adding warm blonde highlights to a bob is one of the easiest ways to breathe new life into your haircut without making a drastic color change. This technique involves weaving golden, honey-toned highlights throughout the hair to create a sunlit effect that brightens the overall look.\n\nOn a bob, these highlights add movement and dimension, making the hair appear fuller and more dynamic. The technique works on both light and dark base colors, though the results will look different depending on your starting shade. Highlights can be placed to frame the face, accentuate layers, or add brightness to the ends for a natural balayage-inspired finish. This is a relatively low-maintenance color option since the highlights blend well as they grow out.\n\nFor a bob that feels fresh, dimensional, and naturally luminous, warm blonde highlights deliver.",
