        "description": "Brunette ombre on a bob creates a beautiful gradient effect that adds dimension and visual interest without the need for constant touch-ups. The color transitions from a darker shade at the roots to a lighter tone at the ends, creating a natural-looking progression that mimics the way hair naturally lightens in the sun.\n\nOn an angled or layered bob, the ombre effect is especially effective because the varying lengths showcase the color transition from multiple angles. This look works well with warm brunette tones like chestnut fading to caramel, or cool tones like espresso melting into ash brown. It is a relatively low-maintenance option since the dark roots blend naturally as the hair grows. For a bob that feels dynamic and full of depth, brunette ombre is a reliable and stylish choice.",
