        "numberTitle": "14. Sleek Glass Hair Bob For Oval Face",
        "image": "assets/bob_haircuts_268_18.jpg",
        "description": "A sleek glass hair bob for an oval face has a bit more flexibility, because this face shape suits many bob lengths and partings. You can choose a jaw-length, chin-length, or longer bob and still maintain flattering proportions, so the main focus becomes how sleek and reflective you want the finish to be.\n\nMany people with oval faces opt for a middle part with a very smooth surface, which emphasizes symmetry and highlights the natural balance of their features. Adding a slight curve under at the ends or leaving them pin straight both work, as long as the overall look remains polished and glassy.\n\nStyling should include a smoothing wash routine, blow-drying with downward tension, and flat ironing in small sections, finishing with a shine spray that keeps the hair glossy without adding heaviness.",
