        "description": "A short blunt bob with side bangs is a smart pick if you want some fringe but prefer it swept away from your face rather than straight across your forehead. The blunt bob keeps everything looking polished and dense at the ends, while side bangs add movement and softness, particularly flattering for square and rectangular face shapes that benefit from diagonal lines crossing the forehead.\n\nThis type of fringe can be cut starting around the eyebrow and stretching toward the cheekbone, which makes blending easy if you later decide to grow it out. Ask your stylist to keep the bob at or slightly above the chin and to angle the side bangs so they fall naturally to one side without a harsh line.\n\nTo style, blow-dry using a round brush to flip the bangs gently across the forehead, then smooth the bob\u2019s ends with a flat iron for a crisp, modern finish.",
