        "numberTitle": "15. Lived In Caramel Blonde With Shadow Root",
        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_225_13.jpg",
        "description": "Lived in caramel blonde with a shadow root leans into contrast in a soft, wearable way. The colorist leaves the root area deeper, often just enhancing your natural shade, and then melts into caramel blonde through the mid-lengths and ends.\n\nThis shadow root diffuses the transition, making the blonde look more modern and less high-maintenance. It is ideal if you love brightness but hate frequent touch-ups because the regrowth blends seamlessly into the existing shadow.\n\nTo keep the look fresh, schedule gloss or toner appointments every couple of months to refine the warmth and refresh shine. At home, stick to color-protecting shampoo and conditioner and limit washing to avoid unnecessary fading.",
