        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_225_5.jpg",
        "description": "A lived in caramel blonde lob pairs shoulder-grazing length with blended, sunlit color that looks chic and effortless. The cut usually sits between the collarbone and shoulders with minimal layers, while the color features a slightly deeper root and caramel blonde highlights through the mid-lengths and ends.\n\nThis combination adds body and movement to the lob, stopping it from feeling heavy or one-dimensional. Style it with a large curling iron or flat iron waves for that undone bend that really shows off the different tones.\n\nTo maintain, ask your colorist for soft balayage retouches a few times a year and trim every eight to ten weeks to keep the ends looking thick and healthy.",
