        "numberTitle": "17. Lived In Caramel Blonde On Curly Hair",
        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_225_9.jpg",
        "description": "On curls, lived in caramel blonde looks incredibly dimensional because every curl and coil reflects light differently. Colorists typically use a balayage approach, painting caramel tones on the outer curls and mid-lengths while respecting the natural pattern and leaving the roots deeper.\n\nThis prevents harsh lines and keeps the curls looking healthy rather than overprocessed. Caramel blonde suits curly hair especially well when paired with a curl-friendly cut, like long layers or a rounded shape that lets the color show throughout.\n\nTo care for colored curls, use sulfate-free, moisture-rich shampoos, deep condition weekly, and minimize direct heat, focusing instead on diffusing or air-drying. A curl cream or lightweight oil helps define the colored strands and reduce frizz.",
