          "It\u2019s especially flattering if you are starting with brown or dark blonde hair and want to go lighter in a gradual, skin-friendly way, because the caramel warmth brightens your complexion while the sandy tones stop the color from turning too yellow. Ask your colorist for a lived-in, rooty finish and focus the lightest pieces around your face and through the lengths, which gives that sun-kissed, beachy effect many salons now describe as \u201clived-in caramel blonde.\u201d With the right sulfate-free shampoo and a blue or purple toning product used every one to two weeks, you can stretch touch-ups to every eight to twelve weeks while keeping the color soft and dimensional instead of flat or brassy."
