        "numberTitle": "6. Sandy Caramel Blonde With Face Framing Layers",
        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_228_16.jpg",
        "description": "Face framing layers combined with sandy caramel blonde color create an instant brightening effect around your features. Your stylist will cut layers that start around the cheekbones or jaw and blend into the rest of your cut, then place sandy caramel highlights strategically on those pieces so they draw attention to your eyes and facial structure.\n\nThe sandy tones keep the blonde near your face from looking too stark against your skin, while the caramel warmth adds a soft glow that can make your complexion look more radiant, especially in natural light. This look works on many lengths\u2014from lobs to long cuts\u2014and can be paired with a shadow root or lived-in base for easy maintenance, as most of the color work is focused near the front rather than all over your head.\n\nUse a heat protectant when styling these layers with a round brush or curling iron, and incorporate shine-enhancing serums or lightweight oils on the mids and ends to showcase the dimension without weighing down the hair.",
