        "numberTitle": "7. Sandy Caramel Blonde For Straight Hair",
        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_228_18.jpg",
        "description": "Straight hair can sometimes make color look one-dimensional, but sandy caramel blonde brings instant depth and interest even without texture. In this look, the colorist places sandy and caramel tones in fine, blended sections so that even when your hair is sleek and straight, you can see subtle ribbons of different shades running through the lengths, especially under bright or daylight conditions.\n\nA slightly deeper root and a mix of mid-tone sandy blonde with lighter caramel accents prevent the overall color from looking flat, which is especially important for fine or medium straight hair that lacks natural volume. Because straight strands show every detail, careful blending and toning are crucial to avoid obvious lines or patchiness, making it worth investing in a skilled colorist and regular gloss appointments.\n\nAt home, use smoothing yet lightweight products, protect your hair from heat with high-quality heat protectant sprays, and consider anti-frizz serums or creams that enhance shine so your sandy caramel blonde looks glossy rather than dull.",
