        "numberTitle": "9. Sandy Caramel Blonde On Fair Skin",
        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_228_14.jpg",
        "description": "On fair skin, sandy caramel blonde brings warmth and dimension without overwhelming delicate complexions, particularly when the sandy base leans slightly cool to balance the richer caramel notes. This combination prevents the color from turning too stark or golden, which can sometimes clash with pink or cool undertones, a concern many blonde color guides address when recommending shades for lighter skin.\n\nYour colorist might keep the root a soft dark blonde or light brown, then blend sandy caramel balayage through the lengths, focusing on softer, finer ribbons of light to avoid a high-contrast, blocked effect. This approach keeps the overall look soft yet radiant, so your hair frames your face with gentle brightness rather than harsh, bright blonde that can wash you out.\n\nProtect your color with UV filters in your hair products, use a gentle purple or blue shampoo when needed to control brass, and avoid overusing hot tools so your lighter lengths remain glossy and healthy on finer hair strands.",
