        "numberTitle": "10. Lived In Sandy Caramel Blonde Hair",
        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_228_2.jpg",
        "description": "On busy days, a lived in sandy caramel blonde look makes it easy to roll out of bed and still feel polished, because the whole color is designed to grow out gracefully and look slightly undone on purpose. Here, your colorist keeps your natural shade or a slightly deepened version at the roots, then blends sandy beige and caramel blonde through the mids and ends with low-contrast transitions, so there\u2019s no obvious line where your color starts or stops.\n\nThe overall effect leans natural and sun-faded, similar to hair that lightened over a long summer, which makes it perfect if you prefer subtle, sophisticated color over very bright blondes. This approach works on straight, wavy, and softly curled textures, and it is especially forgiving for those with warm or neutral undertones in their skin, because the caramel warmth reflects light and adds glow without the maintenance of a full head of foils.\n\nPlan on refreshing your toner and face-framing brightness every two to three months and booking a full balayage or highlight refresh a couple of times a year, while using hydrating masks and color-safe products at home to keep the ends glossy.",
