        "numberTitle": "15. Sandy Caramel Blonde On Medium Skin",
        "image": "assets/warm_blonde_228_13.jpg",
        "description": "Medium skin tones pair beautifully with sandy caramel blonde, which many experts note is a balanced shade\u2014not too warm, not too cool\u2014ideal for subtle yet noticeable change. For this look, your colorist will likely match the warmth level of the caramel to your undertones, leaning slightly warmer if your skin has golden or olive hints, while the sandy tones keep the blonde from looking brassy against your complexion.\n\nSoft balayage or highlights concentrated around the mid-lengths and face can brighten your overall appearance without overpowering your natural coloring, especially if your base is medium brown or dark blonde. Keeping some natural or slightly deepened root visible creates a gentle frame that flatters medium skin, and helps the look stay soft and wearable even as your hair grows out.\n\nMaintain your tone with occasional salon glosses, use color-safe shampoos and conditioners, and incorporate a weekly mask to combat dryness so your sandy caramel blonde stays reflective and smooth rather than dull or frizzy.",
