        "description": "A short wedge haircut for fine thin hair is one of the most effective ways to get the illusion of thicker strands without tons of product. The stacked layers and rounded shape at the back help concentrate volume where fine hair often falls flat\u2014the crown and upper back of the head.\n\nAsk your stylist to keep the nape area slightly tapered and avoid overly long front pieces, which can drag the shape down if your hair is very fine. Layers should be soft but purposeful, with each one slightly shorter than the one beneath it to create a \u201cstacked\u201d effect without choppy steps.\n\nPair the cut with a lightweight volumizing mousse or root spray and blow-dry with your head slightly flipped over to maximize lift. A classic wedge like this can make fine hair appear fuller, especially when combined with subtle highlights that add dimension without damaging the hair too much.",
