        "image": "assets/trending_haircuts_215_6.jpg",
        "description": "A wedge haircut for women over 60 builds on the same flattering principles but leans even more into easy care and gentle volume. This version often sits slightly shorter around the nape and sides, with a soft, curved back that lifts sagging areas visually by drawing the eye upward.\n\nThe top layers are usually kept a bit longer and feathered to allow light movement rather than stiff height, which keeps the look fresh instead of severe. Many stylists recommend pairing this cut with salt and pepper or fully gray hair, as the graduation can make thin areas look fuller. Ask for airier layers instead of dense stacking if your hair is very fine or thinning. This makes the hair easier to style and avoids exposing the scalp.\n\nA soft fringe or side-swept bang can also help disguise forehead lines and bring attention back to your eyes and smile.",
