        "description": "A wedge haircut for women over 50 is an age-inclusive favorite because it offers lift, structure, and a subtle \u201cfacelift\u201d effect without looking too harsh. The key is soft graduation at the back, gentle layering, and face-framing pieces that sit around the cheekbones or chin to highlight your best features.\n\nMany women in this age group appreciate that a wedge removes heavy, dragging ends while still leaving enough length to cover the ears or skim the jaw. It pairs beautifully with gray, silver, or highlighted hair because the layering shows off different tones and adds sparkle around the face.\n\nStyling can stay low-effort: a quick blowout with a round brush or a smooth air-dry with a shaping cream is usually enough to keep the silhouette neat. Regular trims every six to eight weeks help keep the graduation sharp and prevent the shape from collapsing as it grows.",
