        "image": "assets/ponytail_hairstyles_202_5.jpg",
        "description": "A French braid ponytail gives you a secure base that stays put through long lectures and campus walks. Begin with a center or side part, then French braid from your hairline back to the crown, adding sections gradually as you move.\n\nOnce you reach the top back of your head, switch from braiding to gathering the remaining hair into a ponytail and secure it with an elastic. You can keep the ponytail straight, curl the ends, or even braid the tail if your hair is very long.\n\nThis look is great for slightly oily hair days because the braid disguises buildup at the roots and keeps everything neatly contained.",
