        "numberTitle": "3. Loc Ponytail With Beads",
        "image": "assets/ponytail_hairstyles_204_9.jpg",
        "description": "Enhancing your loc ponytail with beads is a classic way to celebrate cultural heritage while adding a bit of rhythmic movement and sound to your style. You can slide wooden, plastic, or metallic beads onto the ends of the locs within the ponytail to create a weighted, decorative finish.\n\nThis look is particularly striking when the ponytail is worn high, as the beads can swing freely and catch the light. It is important to ensure the beads are not too heavy to avoid unnecessary tension on your roots.\n\nChoosing a variety of colors or keeping it monochromatic with gold cuffs can completely change the mood of the hairstyle from playful to regal.",
