        "numberTitle": "3. Low Ponytail With Volume At The Crown",
        "image": "assets/ponytail_hairstyles_210_10.jpg",
        "description": "Adding volume at the crown of your low ponytail gives you a lifted, refreshed look that is perfect for long workdays. The slight elevation prevents your hair from falling flat against your head, which can sometimes make you appear tired.\n\nTo get this look, gently tease the hair at the crown using a fine-tooth comb or teasing brush. Then, smooth the surface layer over the teased section and pull your hair back into a low ponytail.\n\nThe key is to create volume underneath while keeping the top surface smooth and neat. This style works especially well for women with fine or thin hair who want to add the illusion of fullness without using a lot of product.",
