        "image": "assets/ponytail_hairstyles_210_4.jpg",
        "description": "A slicked back high ponytail commands attention without being over the top. It has a bold, confident energy that works well in leadership roles, client meetings, or presentations where you want to project authority.\n\nThe key to making this style office-friendly is keeping the roots flat and smooth with no bumps or lumps. Use a strong-hold gel or pomade and a boar bristle brush to pull every strand upward and backward. Position the ponytail high on the crown of your head and secure it firmly. The lengths should fall straight and smooth behind you.\n\nAvoid excessive teasing or volume on top. The strength of this look comes from its clean, no-nonsense finish.",
