        "numberTitle": "1. Bubble Ponytail For Resort Dinner",
        "image": "assets/ponytail_hairstyles_211_4.jpg",
        "description": "If you want something playful but still dinner-appropriate, a bubble ponytail gives a fun twist to a classic look. Start by creating either a mid or high ponytail and secure it firmly.\n\nThen place small clear elastics every few inches down the length of the ponytail, gently pulling each section outward to create rounded \u201cbubbles.\u201d For a softer resort vibe, keep the bubbles loose rather than exaggerated and avoid over-teasing. A bit of shine spray will help each section catch the light in evening photos. You can leave the top sleek or slightly textured, depending on your outfit and makeup. This look works well on medium to very long hair and is ideal if you want your hairstyle to stand out in a simple maxi dress.\n\nIt\u2019s also surprisingly secure for breezy terraces or outdoor resort restaurants.",
