        "numberTitle": "15. Braided Ponytail For Resort Dinner",
        "image": "assets/ponytail_hairstyles_211_9.jpg",
        "description": "A braided ponytail adds texture and interest while still looking neat for a resort dinner setting. Gather your hair into a mid or high ponytail and secure it firmly, then braid the ponytail into a classic three-strand braid, fishtail, or rope braid.\n\nKeep the braid fairly tight at first, then gently pancake it by pulling at the sides to create a fuller, softer silhouette. This technique stops the braid from looking too severe and gives it a more romantic feel. You can also add a small braid along the hairline that feeds into the ponytail for more detail. Finish with a bit of light-hold hairspray to keep everything in place during dinner.\n\nThis style works especially well on longer hair and looks beautiful with simple, elegant outfits where the hair becomes the main accessory.",
