        "numberTitle": "16. High Polished Ponytail For Resort Dinner",
        "image": "assets/ponytail_hairstyles_211_2.jpg",
        "description": "When you want to look lifted and glamorous at a resort restaurant, a high polished ponytail is a great choice. Brush hair upward from the corners of your eyes toward the crown to find the most flattering height, then secure everything with a tight elastic.\n\nSmoothing gel or pomade along the hairline will control frizz, especially in coastal humidity, while a boar-bristle brush helps you get that glassy finish. Curl the lengths of the ponytail in large, loose waves for extra movement when you walk or turn your head. Wrap a strand of hair around the base to disguise the elastic and pin it underneath. Finish with a light mist of flexible-hold hairspray so it stays polished without looking stiff.\n\nThis works well on medium and long hair, and you can always rely on extensions if you want a truly dramatic length at your resort dinner.",
