        "image": "assets/pastel_hair_color_195_5.jpg",
        "description": "Hidden pastel blue hair has a calm, dreamy vibe that pairs beautifully with cool brunette, black, or icy blonde bases. To get this look, your colorist lightens the underlayer to a pale blonde, then tones it with a pastel blue, often similar to periwinkle or baby blue.\n\nThe blue stays tucked under the natural top, so it is only visible when you twist your hair up, wear pigtails, or curl your ends outward. Pastel blue can sometimes fade toward silver, which actually looks intentional when it is hidden and softly blending with your base color.\n\nThis option is perfect if you want something less common than pink but still soft and wearable. It works best on hair that can safely be lifted light enough for the pastel to show, so bond-protecting treatments and gentle aftercare are key parts of maintaining the overall look.",
