        "image": "assets/pastel_hair_color_195_4.jpg",
        "description": "Hidden pastel purple hair suits anyone who likes a slightly moodier pastel that still reads soft and wearable. Your stylist will create a lightened panel underneath your top layer and apply shades like lilac, soft violet, or dusty lavender to that section only.\n\nThe result is a cool-toned veil of color that peeks out at the ends, around the nape, or through braided sections depending on how you style your hair. Purple looks especially striking under dark brown or black hair because the contrast makes the pastel glow without feeling harsh.\n\nIt is also a great match for ash or cool blonde bases where the tones blend seamlessly. Hidden placement means less exposure to UV and hot tools, so your lilac strands can stay true-toned a little longer before they softly shift toward silvery hues.",
