        "numberTitle": "18. Rose Gold Pink Peekaboo Hair Color",
        "image": "assets/pastel_hair_color_196_4.jpg",
        "description": "Rose gold pink peekaboo color is a great option if you want pink with a more refined, grown\u2011up feel. This shade mixes soft pink with warm golden tones, so it blends beautifully with brown, caramel, or dark blonde bases while still giving a noticeable accent when it peeks through.\n\nYour colorist can place rose gold panels under the top layer from mid\u2011lengths downward, so they show through in curls and layered cuts but hide easily when your hair is straight and down. This look flatters warm and neutral skin tones and works especially well on wavy textures that naturally reveal different tones as they move. Rose gold tends to fade in a pretty way, often shifting to a softer peachy blush instead of going dull. To keep the tone balanced, use sulfate\u2011free shampoo and avoid overly strong purple shampoos that might cool the warmth you want.\n\nA gloss refresh every couple of months helps maintain that polished metallic sheen.",
