        "image": "assets/modern_haircuts_181_17.jpg",
        "description": "Want to add depth back into your lightened hair? The silver lowlights butterfly haircut weaves darker, charcoal-gray pieces into a light metallic base to create stunning visual contrast.\n\nLowlights are the secret to making hair look incredibly thick, as they push certain sections back while allowing the brighter pieces to pop forward. In a butterfly cut, adding lowlights underneath the top layers creates a shadow effect that makes the shorter layers stand out dramatically.\n\nThe darker strands interwoven throughout the lengths prevent the color from looking flat or stringy. It is a fantastic way to keep your heavily layered cut looking robust, three-dimensional, and full of life without adding more bleached highlights.",
