        "numberTitle": "2. Butterfly Haircut For Fine Hair",
        "image": "assets/modern_haircuts_183_10.jpg",
        "description": "Fine hair often struggles to hold a style, but this cut is designed to create the ultimate illusion of density. The butterfly haircut for fine hair relies on strategically placing the shorter layers higher on the head.\n\nThis builds incredible volume at the crown, making the hair appear twice as thick. The longer bottom layers are kept relatively solid to anchor the style and maintain the impression of fullness at the ends.\n\nIt is crucial to avoid over-texturizing fine hair, so the ends are kept cleaner and blunter. A quick blast with a blow-dryer and some volumizing mousse at the roots will give you that coveted bouncy, fluffy finish that lasts all day, even in high humidity.",
