        "description": "The straight hair wolf mullet haircut shows how strong shape and sharp texture can make even smooth hair look dynamic and cool. With straight hair, every layer and line is visible, so the cut focuses on choppy, piecey ends and a defined contrast between the shorter top and longer back.\n\nThe crown gets stacked layers for lift, while the sides stay slightly softer to frame the face and avoid a blocky silhouette. This style works especially well if you have medium to thick straight hair that can hold shape without collapsing.\n\nStyling often involves using a texturizing spray, matte paste, or light wax to rough up the surface and reduce any overly sleek, flat finish. You can blow-dry with a round brush at the crown for extra lift, then smooth or flip the ends slightly for movement, creating a look that feels very modern and fashion editor\u2013approved.",
