        "description": "The wolf mullet haircut with curtain bangs is a softer, more romantic take on this edgy trend, ideal if you want something bold yet wearable. Curtain bangs are parted in the middle and swept to each side, usually starting around the brows and blending into the cheekbones, creating a flattering frame for almost every face shape.\n\nPaired with the layered wolf mullet shape, the curtain fringe softens the strong lines of the cut and gives movement right around the eyes and cheeks. The back and crown still feature choppy layers and a subtle tail, but the overall look feels a bit more polished and nostalgic, reminiscent of vintage rock icons.\n\nStyling focuses on flipping the curtain bangs back with a round brush or flat iron, then enhancing the texture on the rest of the hair with mousse, wave spray, or dry shampoo. This version is especially nice if you like to tuck pieces behind your ears or wear your hair half-up.",
