        "numberTitle": "10. Layered Wolf Mullet Haircut",
        "image": "assets/modern_haircuts_185_9.jpg",
        "description": "The layered wolf mullet haircut is all about maximizing texture and movement for a very full, dimensional look. While every wolf mullet uses layers, this variation leans into them even more, with multiple lengths carved throughout the crown, sides, and back to create a feathered effect.\n\nThis works especially well on thick hair that can handle heavy removal of bulk without looking too thin. The top appears almost fluffy and voluminous, while the back tapers into softer, piecey ends that move easily. Because the layers are so intentional, this version can be customized to flatter your features by placing more volume at the crown, cheeks, or jawline. To style, you usually only need a volumizing spray at the roots and a texture cream worked through the mid-lengths, then a quick rough-dry or air-dry.\n\nThe result is a hairstyle that looks detailed and deliberate even when you put in minimal effort.",
