        "numberTitle": "11. Soft Wolf Mullet Haircut",
        "image": "assets/modern_haircuts_185_14.jpg",
        "description": "The soft wolf mullet haircut is ideal if you like the idea of this trend but don\u2019t want a harsh or extreme look. In this variation, the difference between the shorter crown and longer back is more subtle, with blended layers and gently tapered ends instead of sharp disconnections.\n\nThe overall silhouette still nods to a mullet, but the lines are rounded and flowy rather than edgy. This works beautifully on straight or wavy hair and can be styled to look almost like a layered, modern shag when you wear it forward. Light, face-framing layers and a soft fringe keep the look delicate and flattering. Styling usually involves a bit of shine serum or light cream to emphasize smoothness, plus a quick blowout or gentle wave for movement.\n\nYou still get that cool, trendy feel, but in a way that feels approachable and suitable for a wide range of settings.",
