        "numberTitle": "12. Wolf Mullet Haircut With Bangs",
        "image": "assets/modern_haircuts_185_7.jpg",
        "description": "Adding bangs to a wolf mullet haircut changes the entire mood of the look and helps tailor it to your face shape. This version features a defined fringe in the front\u2014anywhere from soft, eye-grazing bangs to a bolder, straight-across line\u2014while the rest of the hair follows the classic wolf mullet structure with layered sides and a longer back.\n\nBangs help soften a long forehead, balance strong jawlines, or add focus to your eyes, so they make the cut feel more flattering and intentional. You can choose wispy bangs for a light, airy feel, or heavy, full bangs for a stronger statement. Styling typically means blow-drying or straightening the fringe for control, then using texture products through the rest of the hair for that undone finish. The combination of structured bangs and messy lengths creates a cool contrast that looks trendy without feeling overcomplicated.",
