        "description": "For teens who feel like long hair gets in the way but do not want to commit to a true short cut, a short butterfly haircut on medium length hair is a nice middle ground. Hair usually hits between the collarbones and the top of the chest, then is layered heavily around the front and sides to build that signature winged shape.\n\nThis length is easy to wash, dry, and style before school, yet still long enough for half\u2011up looks, claw clips, and low ponytails. The layers bring a lot of movement to medium hair, so even simple straight blow\u2011drying can look intentional and polished instead of flat. If you have fine or medium density hair, asking for soft, graduated layers rather than choppy ones will help keep the ends full while still giving you that lifted, airy finish.",
