          "This creates room for waves or bends to form, so your hair can be styled sleek one day and softly tousled the next without needing a big chop. Because the ghost layers sit underneath, the silhouette stays clean and polished, which is great if you work in a more professional setting or don\u2019t like obvious texture.",
          "On fine or normal hair, this technique gives the illusion of more body around the face and in the sides; on thicker hair, it stops the cut from looking blocky or stiff. It\u2019s a versatile option if you want a mid-length haircut that behaves well in a blowout, a quick air-dry, or loose iron waves."
