        "image": "assets/layered_hairstyles_162_18.jpg",
        "description": "A ghost layers haircut with soft waves might be the most popular combination because the hidden layers give waves a perfect structure to hold onto. When your stylist slices internal layers through the mid-lengths, it creates little pockets of space that allow waves to bend and stack in a very flattering way.\n\nThe outer perimeter remains smooth and full, so your ends don\u2019t look thin even when you add a lot of texture. You can create soft waves with a large curling iron, wand, or even a flat iron, then brush them out for a loose, lived-in finish.\n\nThanks to the ghost layers, the hair naturally separates into gentle, airy pieces instead of one big, solid curl. This style works for medium to long lengths and is ideal for anyone who likes an everyday look that feels relaxed, modern, and easy to dress up or down.",
