        "description": "A ghost layers haircut on a long bob gives you that chic, sharp outline with a lighter, more lived-in interior. The lob typically sits somewhere between the collarbone and upper chest, and many people like it to look straight and polished on the outside.\n\nGhost layers are placed carefully underneath, often concentrated around the crown and mid-lengths, so the hair doesn\u2019t puff out or sit too flat against the head. This lets you wear your lob sleek one day and softly waved the next without seeing harsh layer lines.\n\nBecause fewer ghost layers are used on shorter, hard-lined cuts, the stylist usually takes a conservative approach, focusing on subtle weight removal rather than dramatic internal carving. The result is a long bob that swings, curves, and holds texture more easily, but still looks neat and precise at the edges, which is ideal for both casual and professional settings.",
