        "image": "assets/layered_hairstyles_162_12.jpg",
        "description": "A ghost layers haircut for round face shapes aims to visually elongate and slim the face while keeping hair full and balanced. Stylists usually place more ghost layering around the crown and upper mid-lengths to build height and soft volume on top, which helps offset width in the cheeks.\n\nThe perimeter is often kept below the chin\u2014think shoulder length or longer\u2014to avoid adding bulk right at the widest part of the face. Face-framing pieces may start below the cheekbone and angle downward to create vertical lines that guide the eye up and down instead of side to side.\n\nBecause ghost layers are hidden inside, the ends remain dense enough to look healthy and strong instead of wispy. The overall effect is a haircut that gently narrows and lengthens the appearance of the face without needing extreme layering or a dramatic chop, making it a subtle but effective option.",
