        "numberTitle": "12. Ghost Layers Haircut On Wavy Hair",
        "image": "assets/layered_hairstyles_162_7.jpg",
        "description": "A ghost layers haircut on wavy hair makes it easier to embrace your natural texture while keeping a soft, blended outline. Wavy hair often needs internal shaping so the waves don\u2019t stack up in one area or create a triangle effect, but heavy layers can sometimes lead to frizz and gaps.\n\nGhost layers solve this by carving lightweight internal layers beneath the top section, allowing the waves to interlock in a looser, more even pattern. The outer length remains mostly intact, so you still get a smooth edge at the bottom whether your waves are defined or more relaxed. You can scrunch in a curl cream or mousse and air-dry, and the hidden layers will help the hair expand outward just enough for volume without making the ends look thin. This approach is great if you like switching between natural waves and heat-styled looks because it keeps enough weight for control while adding the texture and lightness that make waves look effortless.",
