        "image": "assets/layered_hairstyles_162_8.jpg",
        "description": "A ghost layers haircut on curly hair focuses on releasing weight and enhancing shape while keeping curls looking dense and healthy. Rather than cutting obvious outer layers that can sometimes create a staircase effect, the stylist works internally, lifting sections and slicing or point-cutting within the horseshoe area or mid-lengths.\n\nThose hidden layers let curls spring up and separate more naturally, especially around the crown where heavy hair can cause flatness. At the same time, the perimeter stays strong, which prevents the ends from appearing too thin or frizzy.\n\nThis technique can be tailored to tighter or looser curl patterns by adjusting how much weight is removed and where, making it flexible for different curl types. With the right curl cream or gel and gentle diffusing, curly hair with ghost layers falls into a more rounded, voluminous shape that still feels under control and doesn\u2019t require a dramatic length sacrifice.",
