        "numberTitle": "17. Ghost Layers Haircut For Fine Hair",
        "image": "assets/layered_hairstyles_162_3.jpg",
        "description": "When you have fine or thin hair, traditional layers can sometimes make the ends look wispy, but a ghost layers haircut for fine hair is designed to avoid that problem. Stylists only layer into the top horseshoe or crown section and leave the bottom layers longer to act as a curtain that hides the shorter pieces underneath.\n\nThis keeps your outline looking solid and full at the ends while still giving your roots and mid-lengths a lift. Because the layers are sliced in diagonally and kept very subtle, the hair gains movement and shape without obvious stair steps or gaps. You can blow-dry with a round brush or use a large curling iron to flip the ends, and the ghost layers will give that extra bounce that fine hair often lacks. If your hair tends to fall flat quickly, this approach adds built-in architecture so volume lasts longer, but you still get the safety of a cut that looks almost one-length when it\u2019s straight and smooth., Effortless Look",
