        "description": "Thick hair can feel heavy and bulky, and many people worry that regular layers will leave them with frizzy ends or too much puff, which is where a ghost layers haircut for thick hair really shines. Instead of carving chunks out of the outer surface, the stylist works underneath, removing weight strategically from interior sections so the hair can move more freely.\n\nThe outer perimeter usually stays blunt or softly rounded, so your hair still appears dense and rich from the outside. This helps avoid that overly layered, piecey look that can make thick hair feel unmanageable.\n\nWith ghost layers, your stylist can customize how much weight is lifted from the crown, sides, or back based on where you tend to feel the most bulk. The result is a cut that dries faster, feels lighter around your neck and shoulders, and holds waves or curls more easily, yet still looks polished and full whether you wear it sleek, air-dried, or softly textured.",
