        "description": "Bright blonde hair pairs beautifully with pastel rainbow underlayers because you already have the light base that pastel shades need to appear soft yet visible. For this look, your top layer can be a creamy or ash blonde with subtle dimension, while the underside is divided into slices or panels and colored in a rainbow order\u2014often pink, peach, yellow, mint, aqua, and lilac\u2014so the tones blend together when you curl or wave your hair.\n\nSince blondes can be more porous, your stylist might choose very diluted semi-permanent dyes, sometimes using a \u201cbubble\u201d technique that allows a bit of blonde to peek through for an airy effect instead of full saturation. This underlayer is perfect if you already wear your hair light and want a low-commitment way to add personality, because the pastels will usually fade gracefully back toward blonde with proper sulfate-free care and lower heat styling.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Bright blonde hair pairs beautifully with pastel rainbow underlayers because you already have the light base that pastel shades need to appear soft yet visible. For this look, your top layer can be a creamy or ash blonde with subtle dimension, while the underside is divided into slices or panels and colored in a rainbow order\u2014often pink, peach, yellow, mint, aqua, and lilac\u2014so the tones blend together when you curl or wave your hair.",
          "Since blondes can be more porous, your stylist might choose very diluted semi-permanent dyes, sometimes using a \u201cbubble\u201d technique that allows a bit of blonde to peek through for an airy effect instead of full saturation. This underlayer is perfect if you already wear your hair light and want a low-commitment way to add personality, because the pastels will usually fade gracefully back toward blonde with proper sulfate-free care and lower heat styling."
        ],
