          "The top layers are slightly longer, then seamlessly blend into shorter layers around the crown and sides, which gives lift and a soft, rounded silhouette. The ends are texturized so they don\u2019t sit in a heavy line, and when you run your fingers through, the hair separates into airy pieces instead of chunky sections. This makes styling easy: a quick blow\u2011dry with a small round brush or even just a bit of volumizing mousse and finger\u2011drying will bring out the feathering. Short feathered layers are especially flattering for people with fine or aging hair, because they visually add body and fullness around the crown and temples. You can wear this cut with a soft side part, slightly pushed\u2011back fringe, or a wispy bang for extra face\u2011framing without committing to a full heavy bang.\u2019ll Love.\u2019ll Love."
