        "image": "assets/layered_hairstyles_167_10.jpg",
        "description": "Long hair often suffers the most from flat, dragging weight. The V cut long hair solves this by creating a distinct\n\nV-shape at the back. The sides are cut shorter and graduate into a longer center point. This removes heavy, dense bulk from the sides while preserving length at the bottom. By taking away this side weight, the top layers naturally lift and expand beautifully.\n\nThe result is gorgeous, cascading volume at the crown with thick, healthy-looking ends. It is the perfect compromise for women who refuse to chop off their length but desperately need to remove the heavy, flat weight.",
