        "numberTitle": "1. Curve Cut Layered Blowout",
        "image": "assets/layered_hairstyles_176_8.jpg",
        "description": "A curve cut layered blowout uses a specific \u201cC-shape\u201d cutting technique where the layers are sculpted to follow the natural curve of the shoulders and jaw. This results in a very soft, rounded silhouette that looks incredibly seamless and fluid.\n\nWhen you blow out a curve cut, the goal is to emphasize these rounded edges by rolling the brush inward at the ends. This creates a \u201cwaterfall\u201d effect where the hair appears to flow smoothly from one layer to the next.\n\nIt is an excellent choice for individuals with fine hair, as the curved layers create the appearance of more density and a thicker hair perimeter without needing excessive products.",
