        "numberTitle": "2. Long Layers For Thin Hair",
        "image": "assets/layered_fine_hair_141_1.jpg",
        "description": "Soft, long layers are a classic way to add movement to thin hair while still keeping the impression of length and fullness through the bottom. The goal is to keep most of the weight near the ends, then add very gentle, blended layers from the mid\u2011shaft down so the hair swings instead of hanging flat.\n\nAsk your stylist for minimal, face\u2011framing pieces that start around the cheekbones or chin, since this draws attention upward and makes your hairline look denser. This kind of long layered cut works especially well if your hair is straight or softly wavy, because the layers are subtle and won\u2019t create thin, feathery strands.\n\nTo style, blow\u2011dry with a round brush or use a large curling iron just on the mid\u2011lengths, leaving the ends slightly straighter for a modern finish that keeps the hair looking thick, not wispy.",
