        "description": "A layered shag is perfect if your thin hair always seems to lie flat and you want more texture and movement throughout the whole cut. This haircut uses lots of choppy, feathered layers to break up the length and encourage natural bend, which instantly makes hair look fuller.\n\nFor fine hair, modern shags are usually softer and more blended than the dramatic versions from the past, so you get volume without harsh steps. The layers are often concentrated around the crown and mid\u2011lengths, leaving just enough weight at the ends to stop the hair from looking too wispy.\n\nA shag thrives with a bit of texture spray, air\u2011drying, or a diffuser, making it a good match if you like an undone, lived\u2011in finish. You can pair it with bangs or keep the front slightly longer and shaggy to suit your face shape and styling comfort level.",
