        "numberTitle": "14. Textured Layers With Modern Bangs",
        "image": "assets/layered_fine_hair_141_13.jpg",
        "description": "Combining textured layers with modern bangs is a smart way to give thin hair instant personality and the illusion of thickness around the face. The bangs are usually soft and slightly piecey, falling somewhere between full fringe and wispy curtain bangs for a wearable, low\u2011maintenance look.\n\nThroughout the rest of the hair, light layers add movement without creating a see\u2011through effect at the ends, which is crucial for fine strands. This combination looks especially flattering when styled with loose waves or a relaxed blowout, since the texture helps the bangs blend into the rest of the cut.\n\nAsk your stylist to keep the fringe airy rather than blunt so it does not feel too heavy or flat on thinner hairlines. A small amount of dry shampoo or volumizing powder at the roots of your bangs can keep them lifted throughout the day.",
