        "numberTitle": "15. Asymmetrical Bob With Layers For Thin Hair",
        "image": "assets/layered_fine_hair_141_12.jpg",
        "description": "An asymmetrical bob with layers gives thin hair a modern, fashion\u2011forward twist while still delivering the volume you want. One side is usually slightly longer than the other, which tricks the eye and makes the whole style look more dynamic and full.\n\nLayers are kept soft and strategic, often focusing on the longer side and around the crown so the hair lifts away from the scalp. For fine hair, this cut works well when the perimeter stays relatively strong, avoiding overly thin ends that could make the difference in length too extreme.\n\nYou can part your hair deeply on one side to exaggerate the angle and create even more height at the roots. This style suits both straight and wavy textures and can be worn sleek for a professional setting or tousled for a more relaxed, playful look.",
