        "image": "assets/layered_fine_hair_141_4.jpg",
        "description": "A soft layered bob gives thin hair instant structure while avoiding the overly stacked, choppy look that can sometimes highlight sparse ends. This cut usually sits between the chin and the jaw or slightly lower, with gentle layers that add movement without removing too much weight from the perimeter.\n\nBy keeping the bottom line relatively full and just softening the interior, the hair looks thicker, especially from the side. It is a great choice if you like a neat, polished appearance but still want your hair to feel airy rather than heavy.\n\nAsk your stylist to avoid aggressive thinning shears and to focus on light texturizing instead, particularly around the ends and face. This bob looks beautiful blown out with a round brush, but it also works air\u2011dried with a little texture cream for a relaxed, everyday finish.",
