        "description": "A long layered haircut with a lifted side part is a simple way to give thin hair more height and a fuller appearance around the face. By shifting the part to one side, you instantly create extra volume at the roots on the heavier side of the hair.\n\nThe layers themselves should be soft and graduated, focusing on adding shape around the front and through the mid\u2011lengths. This keeps the silhouette flowing while avoiding overly thin ends at the back. For fine hair, a deep side part paired with a gentle wave can make a big difference in how thick the hair looks overall. It is also a flexible choice because you can always return to a center part or adjust the placement when you want something different.\n\nA root\u2011lifting spray or quick round\u2011brush blowout at the front helps maintain that lifted, voluminous effect.",
