        "numberTitle": "1. Layered Lob Fine Hair",
        "image": "assets/layered_fine_hair_153_19.jpg",
        "description": "The \u201clob,\u201d or long bob, is a classic for a reason, and adding layers makes it even better for fine hair. A layered lob typically hits right at the collarbone, which is a very flattering length for most people.\n\nBy adding layers throughout, you prevent the hair from looking too heavy at the bottom. This keeps the volume balanced from the roots to the tips. It is a very versatile cut that can be worn sleek and professional or messy and casual. The length is perfect for those who want to keep some hair to play with but want the ease of a shorter style.\n\nIt remains a top-tier choice for modern women everywhere.",
