        "numberTitle": "6. Ash Bronde With Auburn Undertones",
        "image": "assets/doc_cool_balayage_8.jpg",
        "description": "Ash tones have been dominating the hair color scene for years, but adding hidden auburn undertones creates a version that feels fresh and modern. Ash bronde with auburn undertones starts with a cool, smoky brown base that transitions into muted blonde ends, but subtle copper and mahogany lowlights peek through when the hair moves or catches direct light.\n\nThe cooler base keeps the look sophisticated and understated, while the auburn tones add a surprising layer of warmth that prevents the color from looking flat or washed out. This is an excellent choice for those with cool or neutral skin tones who want to dabble in red tones without going full copper.",
