        "image": "assets/doc_cool_balayage_10.jpg",
        "description": "Face-framing highlights are a subtler, more blended version of the money piece, and in auburn bronde tones they create a soft, glowing halo around the face. Instead of thick blocks of color, fine pieces of copper gold and warm blonde are painted along the hairline and parted sections, gradually fading into the natural base color.\n\nThe effect is like having a permanent golden-hour glow around your face at all times. This look is incredibly versatile and works on every hair length from a short pixie to floor-length waves.\n\nIt also requires very little maintenance since the highlights blend seamlessly into the rest of your hair as they grow out.",
