        "image": "assets/doc_b_27_16.jpg",
        "description": "Chestnut balayage for cool skin tone takes a slightly different path by choosing neutral to cool chestnut shades that avoid too much yellow or orange warmth. Colorists may lean into mocha chestnut, neutral chestnut, or chestnut mixed with soft ash tones to keep the overall effect balanced.\n\nThe balayage is still painted in a natural, sun-kissed pattern, but the lighter sections stay within a cooler range so they harmonize with pink or rosy undertones. This helps prevent your skin from looking flushed or overly warm next to your hair.\n\nStyled straight or with gentle waves, cool-friendly chestnut balayage reads as polished, sophisticated, and modern, particularly if you prefer silver jewelry and cooler shades in your wardrobe.",
