        "image": "assets/doc_b_27_1.jpg",
        "description": "Think of classic chestnut balayage on long hair as the go-to look when you want movement and shine without giving up your length. Colorists usually start with a medium to dark brown base, then hand-paint ribbons of warm chestnut and soft caramel from mid-lengths through the ends, concentrating brighter pieces near the face for a glow effect.\n\nThe transition stays gradual, so you see a melt rather than a harsh line, which is what keeps this look chic and salon-fresh even as it grows out. Soft waves or a bend created with a curling iron help show off every shade, making the lighter chestnut sections pop in natural or indoor light.\n\nThis version is perfect if you love a timeless, flattering color that feels polished but still easy to style day to day.",
