        "numberTitle": "6. Low Maintenance Chestnut Balayage",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_27_17.jpg",
        "description": "Low maintenance chestnut balayage is all about soft regrowth and easy upkeep while still enjoying a noticeable color upgrade. Colorists typically keep your natural root color, then blend chestnut balayage starting several inches down, creating a shadow root effect that grows out seamlessly.\n\nThe chestnut tones are chosen close to your base shade, so even as your hair grows, there is no harsh line between old and new color. This means you can stretch salon visits to every few months instead of every few weeks, which saves both time and budget.\n\nWhen styled in relaxed waves, braids, or simple blowouts, this kind of balayage always looks intentional and lived-in, rather than like you are overdue for an appointment.",
