        "image": "assets/doc_b_27_18.jpg",
        "description": "Chestnut balayage with glossy finish turns up the shine factor so your color looks rich and reflective. After creating the balayage, many stylists apply a demi-permanent gloss or toner in a chestnut shade to even out the tones and add high shine.\n\nThis gloss can neutralize unwanted warmth, deepen the chestnut, or add specific reflects like gold or neutral bronze depending on your goal. The result is hair that looks smoother and healthier, with light bouncing off the chestnut ribbons for a mirror-like effect.\n\nUsing color-safe, shine-enhancing shampoos and conditioners at home helps maintain that glossy finish between appointments, making your chestnut balayage look freshly done for longer.",
