        "image": "assets/doc_b_32_20.jpg",
        "description": "Do you struggle with your hair turning orange or brassy every time you get highlights? Cool toned balayage on brown hair uses icy browns and pale mushrooms to keep things crisp.\n\nThis technique is all about neutralizing warmth to achieve a clean, modern look. It is perfect for people who have cool or olive skin tones. Cool-toned highlights look very sophisticated and expensive. They create a beautiful contrast against a dark brown base without looking unnatural. This style is often achieved using a toner after the initial lightening process. It keeps your hair looking fresh and salon-quality for a long time.\n\nYou can style this with a sleek ponytail for a very chic look.",
