        "image": "assets/doc_b_35_14.jpg",
        "description": "Long hair gives balayage with root shadow maximum room to shine. The length allows for a gradual, sweeping gradient \u2014 a deep, rich root that slowly transitions through mid-lengths into bright, dimensional ends.\n\nThis creates a beautiful, almost ombr\u00e9-like effect while still maintaining the softness and blending that separates balayage from harsh color blocking. Long hair in this technique can carry multiple tones \u2014 warm mid-lengths and cooler ends, for example \u2014 adding incredible depth and movement. The longer the hair, the more dramatic the payoff. It\u2019s also highly photogenic, especially on straight or loosely styled hair where the full color gradient is clearly visible.\n\nRegular glossing treatments and bond-building products help keep long, color-treated hair healthy and luminous.",
