        "description": "Curly hair with balayage and root shadow is genuinely stunning \u2014 and surprisingly manageable. Curls naturally diffuse color, so the balayage creates a softly sun-kissed effect across the curl pattern rather than sharp highlights.\n\nThe root shadow keeps the scalp area rich and deep, adding contrast that makes each curl look defined and dimensional. Because curly hair tends to be drier, colorists usually opt for a demi-permanent root shadow and a gentle balayage lift to minimize damage. The result is luminous, healthy-looking curls with beautiful color depth. Whether you have loose waves or tight coils, this technique adapts wonderfully.\n\nUse a moisturizing leave-in conditioner and a curl-enhancing cream to keep color-treated curls hydrated, bouncy, and vibrant between washes.",
