        "description": "Starting from a brown base and going platinum balayage is a dramatic transformation \u2014 but the results are absolutely worth it. The contrast between the warm brown base and the cool, icy platinum creates a stunning high-contrast look full of depth and dimension.\n\nThe balayage technique is especially useful here because it allows the colorist to gradually lighten sections without making the transition look harsh or abrupt. Instead, you get a smooth, organic-looking blend that feels natural.\n\nBrown-haired women opting for this look often keep some warmth at the roots and lower base sections, which makes the platinum tones at the mid-lengths and ends look even brighter by comparison. Purple shampoo is a must for maintaining the icy tones and preventing brassiness on a brown-to-platinum balayage.",
