        "numberTitle": "13. Beige Blonde Highlights On Brown Hair With Layers",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_40_13.jpg",
        "description": "Layered brown hair becomes more textured and airy with beige blonde highlights placed along the lengths of each layer. Your stylist may paint lighter pieces on the ends of shorter layers and through the mid-lengths of longer ones, enhancing the haircut\u2019s movement.\n\nBeige tones keep everything cohesive, preventing the layers from reading choppy or overly streaky. This look suits many cuts, from shag-inspired layers to softer, face-framing ones, and works well with blowouts and waves.\n\nAsk your colorist to show you how the color and layers work together when styling, then maintain at home with volumizing yet color-safe products so your layers lift without drying out the highlighted strands.",
