        "numberTitle": "14. Beige Blonde Ribbon Highlights On Brown Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_40_18.jpg",
        "description": "Ribbon highlights create thicker, flowing streaks of beige blonde that wind through brown hair like ribbons. Your colorist places them in a way that follows the natural fall and movement of your hair, often using foils or a combination of foils and balayage.\n\nThe beige tone softens the larger pieces, so they look dimensional rather than stripy. This technique looks especially beautiful on longer haircuts and layered styles where the ribbons can be seen from all angles.\n\nMaintain the smooth look of these larger highlighted sections with regular conditioning treatments and gentle detangling, as rough brushing or tight hairstyles can cause breakage along the more heavily lightened pieces.",
