        "numberTitle": "18. Dimensional Beige Blonde Highlights On Brown Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_40_20.jpg",
        "description": "Dimensional beige blonde highlights on brown hair combine different highlight sizes and placements for a rich, multi-layered result. Your colorist may mix babylights, a few chunkier pieces, and some balayage on the ends, all toned in complementary beige shades.\n\nThis blend mimics the kind of natural variation you see in hair that has been lightened by the sun over time. The brown base peeks through in some areas while others look brighter, giving your hair movement and interest from every angle.\n\nTo preserve this complexity, schedule regular glosses and trims, and avoid harsh clarifying shampoos that can strip the toner and make the beige look flat or overly warm too quickly.",
