        "image": "assets/doc_b_48_12.jpg",
        "description": "If you\u2019re not ready for a full single-process color, espresso mocha ombre is the perfect compromise. This look keeps a deep, near-black espresso tone at the roots and transitions gradually into a warmer, slightly lighter mocha shade through the ends.\n\nThe result is a seamless gradient that looks incredibly dimensional and natural \u2014 like your hair has been naturally sun-lightened at the tips. It works on any length but looks especially stunning on long, wavy or curly hair where the color transition can fully show off its range. Gemma Chan\u2019s dark chocolate-to-mocha ombre is a great reference point: deep and dramatic at the root, softer and warmer toward the ends.\n\nMaintenance is easy because the ombre placement sits away from the root, meaning less frequent salon trips.",
