        "description": "Molten brunette is one of the most buzzed-about dark roast brunette variations of the moment \u2014 and for good reason. It blends chocolate, amber, and mocha shades together to create the illusion of light moving through your strands, giving hair a fluid, almost prismatic shimmer.\n\nVogue named it fall and winter\u2019s most luxurious hair color trend, noting that the effect looks like molten metal \u2014 rich, radiant, and deeply dimensional. What sets it apart from standard dark brown is the subtle multi-dimensionality: it\u2019s not a flat color, but it\u2019s not obviously highlighted either. It reads as a rich, glowing singular tone that reflects winter light beautifully. This shade suits both golden skin tones and porcelain complexions, making it one of the most universally flattering options in the dark brunette world.\n\nLow maintenance is another huge selling point \u2014 no frequent highlight touch-ups needed.",
