        "numberTitle": "20. Dark Roast Brunette with Caramel Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_48_10.jpg",
        "description": "Adding caramel highlights to a dark roast brunette base is one of the most sought-after looks in salons right now \u2014 and it\u2019s easy to see why. The warm, golden caramel tones create just enough contrast against the deep brown base to add life and dimension without veering into bronde territory.\n\nThis look works beautifully on long, layered hair where the highlights can trace the movement and fall naturally around the face. It frames your complexion with warmth and brightness, almost like a natural filter. The key is keeping the caramel pieces soft and blended \u2014 not chunky or stripy. Balayage application with a root shadow keeps the transition from dark roots to light ends completely seamless.\n\nA color gloss afterward unifies everything into a rich, cohesive finish.",
