        "image": "assets/doc_b_48_9.jpg",
        "description": "Mocha brown balayage is perfect for anyone who wants to keep their dark base but add a little warmth and movement. The technique involves hand-painting soft, warm brown tones through the mid-lengths and ends, creating a sun-kissed effect that looks totally natural.\n\nWhat makes this version special is the mocha tone \u2014 it\u2019s warmer than plain brown but softer than caramel, sitting right in that sweet spot of dimensional brunette color. Kaia Gerber\u2019s espresso-to-mocha balayage is a great real-world reference: dark roots melt seamlessly into a slightly lighter, glossy mocha finish. This look is very low maintenance since the grow-out blends naturally with your roots.\n\nA gloss treatment every 6\u20138 weeks keeps the warmth looking fresh and vibrant.",
