        "numberTitle": "25. Dimensional Mocha Brunette Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_48_15.jpg",
        "description": "Dimensional mocha brunette is all about creating the illusion of depth and movement without looking obviously colored. A deep brunette base gets overlaid with ribbons of warm caramel and mid-toned mocha, resulting in a kissed-by-the-sun appearance that\u2019s multi-layered and rich.\n\nColorist Michael Rincon explains it perfectly: start with a deep brunette base, apply subtle highlights, then gloss with the same base tone to tie everything together for that seamless shimmer in the light. This is actually one of the most popular brunette requests in salons right now because it gives the visual complexity of heavily highlighted hair while still reading as a natural, cohesive brunette. It works on all hair textures and lengths.\n\nLori Harvey\u2019s single-process mocha with a subtle gloss finish is one of the most-referenced examples of this look done perfectly.",
