        "numberTitle": "19. Silver Ribbons In Light Brown Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_64_8.jpg",
        "description": "Adding silver ribbons in light brown hair creates a soft, ethereal look that feels almost like a \u201cbronde\u201d but with a metallic twist. This combination is less about high contrast and more about creating a shimmering, multi-dimensional texture.\n\nThe light brown base provides a warm enough foundation to prevent the silver from looking too stark, resulting in a creamy, toasted silver finish. This is a great transition color for blondes who want to go darker or brunettes who want to go lighter without dealing with yellow or brassy undertones.\n\nIt looks best with plenty of movement, so consider pairing this color with a layered haircut or a shaggy lob to let the ribbons dance.",
