        "image": "assets/doc_b_65_5.jpg",
        "description": "Deep, bold roots paired with warm, melting ends \u2014 the espresso to soft caramel ombre is a stunning take on classic brown ombre that leans on dramatic depth for visual impact. Espresso is one of the richest, darkest shades of brown, and when it gradually transitions into a warm caramel, the result is luxurious and multi-dimensional.\n\nThe contrast between the near-black roots and the lighter caramel tips creates natural depth that makes hair look thick and full. This style holds up especially well on long hair, where each color phase gets ample room to shine.\n\nIt suits all skin tones beautifully and requires minimal root maintenance, since the roots stay dark intentionally. Touch-up appointments are typically needed only every 12 to 16 weeks.",
