        "image": "assets/doc_b_69_9.jpg",
        "description": "Face-framing highlights are a targeted, strategic approach to gray blending that focuses brightness exactly where you need it most, around your hairline and face. This technique involves placing lighter pieces along the front sections of your hair, which is often where gray strands first appear and where they are most visible.\n\nBy highlighting this zone with cool blonde or ash tones, your grays blend right in and the overall look stays fresh and polished. The rest of your hair can remain closer to your natural brown, which keeps the maintenance low and the change subtle.\n\nFace-framing highlights also have a flattering effect, brightening your complexion and drawing attention to your eyes and features. This is an excellent entry point for brunettes who are new to gray blending and want to test the waters before committing to a full-head technique.",
