          "Techniques like balayage, smudged roots, and soft babylights are common here, because they create \u201ccolor within color\u201d and subtle contrast rather than stark stripes. You can choose warmer tones like caramel or toffee or go more neutral depending on your undertone, and your colorist can customize glosses that make fading more forgiving.",
