        "numberTitle": "8. Brunette With Mushroom Brown Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_14.jpg",
        "description": "Mushroom brown highlights give brunette hair a trend-forward, cool-toned dimension with hints of taupe, beige, and soft ash. This look is ideal if you prefer muted, sophisticated shades over warm golds or reds.\n\nThe highlights are usually painted as balayage or foilyage in varying levels of cool beige and smoky brown, creating a multi-tonal effect that almost looks like natural shadow and light. Mushroom brown works particularly well on medium to dark brunettes and cooler or neutral complexions.\n\nBecause cool tones can shift warmer over time, use color-safe, sulfate-free products and occasional blue-based toning solutions approved for brunette hair, and protect your color from heat and sun exposure, which both speed up fading and can reveal unwanted warmth underneath the carefully created cool overlay.",
