        "numberTitle": "9. Dark Brown Hair With Chestnut Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_3.jpg",
        "description": "Chestnut highlights are a beautiful choice when you want dimension without a big jump in level, especially on dark brown hair. The chestnut tone sits only slightly lighter than the natural base and adds a mix of warm brown and subtle red reflects that glow in the sun.\n\nThis look usually focuses on mid-lengths and ends, with a few chestnut pieces diffused through the crown to keep the color looking rich rather than streaky. Because the contrast is mild, regrowth is soft, making it a practical option if you prefer less frequent salon visits.\n\nChestnut highlights also help curly or wavy textures look more defined, since the lighter pieces emphasize each bend and coil. Maintain the color with sulfate-free products and occasional shine-enhancing glosses to keep that polished finish.",
