        "numberTitle": "10. Brunette With Dimensional Lowlights And Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_20.jpg",
        "description": "Combining lowlights and highlights in brunette hair creates maximum dimension, making the hair appear thicker and more multi-tonal. In this look, slightly darker lowlights are woven in to restore depth where needed, while lighter highlights add brightness on the surface and around the face.\n\nThe contrast is kept moderate so everything blends into a cohesive, natural-looking brunette rather than obvious stripes. This approach is especially helpful if your hair has been over-lightened and you want to return to a more natural brunette while still keeping some lightness.\n\nAt home, maintain the balance by using color-safe products that protect both the darker and lighter tones, and schedule periodic gloss appointments to refresh shine and keep the overall color story rich, dimensional, and flattering to your features.",
