        "numberTitle": "11. Brunette With Baby Blonde Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_16.jpg",
        "description": "Baby blonde highlights on brunette hair create a higher-contrast, yet still delicate, effect using very fine, pale strands throughout the top layers. The technique takes its name from the soft, natural blonde of children\u2019s hair, which is why the pieces are micro-fine and carefully blended.\n\nOn a brunette base, these highlights are often concentrated near the front and crown, with the underlayers left darker to keep the look grounded. This combination can give the illusion of thicker, more voluminous hair because the light pieces sit on top of the deeper background.\n\nBecause baby blonde requires lifting to a lighter level, it is essential to pair the color with bond-protecting treatments, heat protection, and regular trims, and to visit the salon for toners when needed to keep the blonde looking creamy instead of yellow.",
