        "numberTitle": "12. Brunette With Subtle Teasylight Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_19.jpg",
        "description": "Subtle teasylights use backcombing before applying lightener to create the softest, most diffused brunette highlights possible. This technique is ideal if you want a very natural finish with no visible lines or chunky pieces.\n\nThe colorist teases sections at the root, paints lightener on the ends and mid-lengths, then lets the teased hair create a natural blur so the highlights blend seamlessly into the base. Once toned, the result is a whisper of brightness that shows mainly in movement and sunlight.\n\nBecause the lift is usually gentle and the pieces are soft, maintenance can be spaced out, focusing instead on at-home care like hydrating masks, bond-building products when recommended, and protecting the hair from heat so the lightweight highlights stay smooth and do not fray at the ends.",
