        "numberTitle": "15. Brunette With Golden Brown Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_18.jpg",
        "description": "Golden brown highlights are a classic way to brighten brunette hair while keeping the overall tone soft, warm, and wearable. The shade sits comfortably between caramel and light brown, adding a sunlit feel that works for many skin tones, especially those with warm undertones.\n\nPlacement usually focuses on the outer layers, lengths, and ends, with a few brighter pieces near the face to lift the complexion. Because the highlights are not drastically lighter than the base, the result is low-contrast and easy to maintain.\n\nTo keep golden brown from shifting too brassy, stick to color-protective products, consider occasional toning, and avoid excessive heat styling, which can roughen the cuticle and make warm tones look dull instead of glowing and dimensional on your brunette base.",
