        "numberTitle": "16. Brunette With Soft Ombre Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_9.jpg",
        "description": "Soft ombre highlights, sometimes called sombr\u00e9, create a gradual transition from a deeper brunette root to lighter ends without a stark break in color. This technique is ideal if you like the brightness at your ends but want minimal maintenance at the root.\n\nThe colorist typically starts the lighter shade a few inches below the root, blending it downward using teasing or balayage to avoid lines. For a natural result, the ombre tones can be caramel, honey, or soft bronde, chosen based on your skin undertone and how much lift your hair can handle.\n\nBecause the root stays largely untouched, you can stretch appointments, focusing instead on conditioning masks, bond-building treatments, and occasional toners on the ends to keep the gradient smooth and the lighter pieces glossy and healthy.",
