        "numberTitle": "17. Brunette With Beige Blonde Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_8.jpg",
        "description": "Beige blonde highlights on brunette hair strike a balance between warm and cool, giving a soft, refined brightness without looking too golden or ashy. This look is especially flattering on neutral or slightly cool skin tones and can make brown eyes appear lighter and more defined.\n\nThe beige tone is usually applied as balayage or foilyage, focusing on mid-lengths and ends with a few fine pieces near the face, so the overall effect is dimensional but smooth. Because beige is a subtle, sophisticated shade, it tends to photograph beautifully in natural and indoor lighting.\n\nTo keep the beige from drifting too warm or dull, use color-protective products and occasional toning treatments recommended for neutral blondes, and limit hot tool usage so the hair\u2019s cuticle remains smooth and reflective.",
