        "numberTitle": "18. Brunette With Bronde Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_15.jpg",
        "description": "Bronde highlights blend brunette and blonde tones so seamlessly that it can be hard to tell where one ends and the other begins. This look offers the brightness of blonde with the depth of brunette, making it a popular choice for anyone who wants a noticeable change that still feels wearable.\n\nThe colorist typically uses balayage or foilyage to weave multiple tones\u2014caramel, beige blonde, and medium brown\u2014through the hair, focusing on mid-lengths and ends with a softer root. The result is highly dimensional, glossy, and flattering on many skin tones.\n\nTo keep bronde looking intentional instead of brassy, follow a routine of color-protective cleansing, weekly treatments, and periodic toning or gloss services that refresh both the brunette depth and the blonde lightness while maintaining a smooth, reflective surface on the hair.",
