        "numberTitle": "20. Brunette With Mocha Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_74_13.jpg",
        "description": "Mocha highlights are a chic, understated way to enhance dark brunette hair with cool or neutral depth rather than overt warmth. The color mixes chocolate and subtle ash or neutral tones, creating a smoky dimension that is especially flattering on cooler skin tones.\n\nThis technique usually uses low-contrast ribbons just a shade or two lighter than the base, woven throughout the crown and ends to give movement and shine. The result looks expensive and polished, with no harsh lines or overly bright pieces.\n\nBecause mocha is more about tone than lightness, maintenance revolves around preserving that cool balance by avoiding overly warm hair products and occasionally using a gentle blue or purple-toned product recommended for brunettes, plus regular conditioning to keep the hair smooth and light-reflective.",
