        "description": "Blending caramel and honey balayage on brunette hair creates a layered warmth that feels rich but still multi-tonal. Caramel brings that brownish-gold depth, while honey adds slightly lighter, more golden touches for extra brightness.\n\nYour colorist might use caramel for most of the mid-lengths and tuck honey accents closer to the face and ends. This combination is great if you want more lift than caramel alone but still prefer warm, flattering tones over cool blondes.\n\nThe mix can also help soften a naturally cooler or ashy brunette base, giving your complexion more radiance. To preserve both shades, use hydrating, color-safe products and ask for a custom gloss that refreshes caramel and honey in one quick salon visit.",
