        "numberTitle": "7. Warm Caramel Balayage Maintenance For Brunette Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_75_20.jpg",
        "description": "Once you have your dream caramel balayage, proper maintenance keeps it looking glossy and fresh. Warm shades can shift brassy over time, so using a color-safe, sulfate-free shampoo and a nourishing conditioner is essential.\n\nMany pros recommend periodic in-salon or at-home gloss treatments to revive richness and add shine between big appointments. Deep conditioning masks and bond-repair products help counteract dryness from lightening, especially on mid-lengths and ends.\n\nTry to limit heat styling, always use heat protectant, and avoid very hot water when washing your hair. Following your stylist\u2019s personalized care plan will help your warm caramel balayage stay soft, dimensional, and flattering for months instead of fading quickly.",
