        "image": "assets/doc_b_75_2.jpg",
        "description": "If you like the idea of caramel but worry about going too light, subtle caramel balayage on dark brown hair is a gentle starting point. Your colorist will paint fine, diffused caramel pieces just one to two levels lighter than your natural shade for a soft glow instead of strong contrast.\n\nThe highlights sit mostly in the mid-lengths, with a few delicate pieces near the face, so your overall look still reads as brunette. Because the difference between base and highlight is small, regrowth is almost invisible, which makes this option very low-maintenance.\n\nThis is perfect for anyone in a professional setting or someone coloring their hair for the first time. A glossy finish or in-shower color gloss helps keep the caramel tones shiny and rich between appointments.",
