        "description": "Face framing caramel balayage is a flattering choice if you love dimension right where the light naturally hits your hair. With this look, the colorist paints caramel highlights around your face and through the top layer, leaving the interior slightly deeper for rich contrast.\n\nThis placement makes your eyes and cheekbones stand out, and it can even soften strong features. Because the highlights hug the front and crown, the color looks vibrant in photos and in real life without needing all-over lightening.\n\nIt works especially well with layered cuts, curtain bangs, or soft waves that move around the face. Ask your stylist to keep the transitions diffused and avoid harsh lines at the root so the grow-out stays soft and manageable between touch-ups.",
