        "numberTitle": "10. Low Maintenance Caramel Balayage For Brunettes",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_75_19.jpg",
        "description": "If you want to stretch time between appointments, ask for low maintenance caramel balayage designed around your natural root. Your colorist will keep your root area mostly untouched, focusing the lightness on mid-lengths and ends with soft, feathered strokes.\n\nA root shadow or smudge can further blur any transition so regrowth blends in effortlessly. This approach works especially well for busy people or anyone on a budget who still wants dimensional color.\n\nYou can adjust how bright or subtle the caramel is while keeping the upkeep schedule relaxed. Use color-safe shampoo, limit hot tools, and schedule occasional gloss appointments to refresh tone rather than full lightening sessions every visit.",
