        "numberTitle": "1. Voluminous Curled Ends Blowout",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_79_6.jpg",
        "description": "If you love a classic blowout but want the drama focused at the bottom, a voluminous curled ends blowout is a smart pick. This look keeps the roots and mid-lengths smoother and closer to the head, then concentrates bounce and curl through the lower third of the hair for swingy, playful movement.\n\nCelebrities often wear this with off-the-shoulder dresses or sleek necklines so the ends can sit on top of the fabric and really show off the rounded shape. The style is usually created with a round brush or large curling iron on big sections, then brushed together to create one unified, full curve.\n\nSet with a light hairspray and a little shine spray, it gives that polished, red carpet feel while still being easy to touch up or refresh the next day.",
