        "numberTitle": "3. 90s Supermodel Blowout",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_79_1.jpg",
        "description": "Think of those iconic campaign shots of Cindy Crawford or Naomi Campbell, with huge, bouncy hair that moves with every step.\n\nThis 90s supermodel blowout is all about big, rounded volume from roots to ends, smooth texture, and a soft bend that looks expensive but not stiff. The cut usually works best on medium to long hair with long layers, so the ends don\u2019t look heavy or blocky when you brush everything out.\n\nTo copy the look, stylists prep with a volumizing mousse and heat protectant, then use a round brush to lift at the roots and curl sections away from the face before setting the hair to cool. Once brushed through, it frames the face with a glamorous, high-impact finish that still feels wearable with jeans or a gown.",
