        "image": "assets/doc_b_79_14.jpg",
        "description": "Dua Lipa\u2019s bright cherry red era made colorful blowouts feel edgy yet polished.\n\nA cherry red blowout usually pairs a vivid, saturated red or deep cherry tone with a sleek or softly wavy finish that lets the color stay in focus. The hair may be worn with a center part and smooth texture or with a gentle bend added via round brush or curling tool, then brushed out for movement.\n\nStylists often use color-protecting products and shine sprays to keep the red from looking dull, and they avoid heavy, powdery sprays that could cast a haze over the shade. The result feels like a pop star moment that still fits everyday outfits, especially if you like pairing statement hair with simple lines and clean, minimal styling on clothes and makeup.",
