        "numberTitle": "13. Ginger Copper Balayage on Brunette",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_85_3.jpg",
        "description": "Ginger and copper together create one of the most eye-catching combinations in the hair color world. When applied as a balayage over a brunette base, those bright ginger ribbons weave through the hair like threads of pure sunlight.\n\nThis look gives off major autumn energy, resembling the warm hues of falling leaves and spiced lattes. The key to nailing this shade is finding the right balance between the base color and the highlights. Too much ginger can overwhelm darker hair, while too little might not show up at all. A skilled colorist will paint the ginger pieces strategically, focusing on the areas where light naturally hits your hair.\n\nThe end result is a vibrant yet natural-looking warmth that makes people stop and stare.",
