        "numberTitle": "15. Copper Balayage on Curly Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_85_15.jpg",
        "description": "Curly hair and copper balayage were practically made for each other. The natural coils and spirals of curly hair create a stunning visual effect when painted with bright copper ribbons.\n\nEach curl becomes a tiny showcase of dimension, with the copper tones weaving in and out of the natural base color. The result is a head full of bouncing, vibrant, multi-tonal ringlets that look absolutely breathtaking. Curly hair also tends to reflect light differently than straight hair, which means copper balayage on curls often appears more saturated and rich. The color enhances the natural texture rather than fighting against it.\n\nWhether your curls are loose and flowing or tight and coily, copper balayage adds warmth and definition that makes every single curl stand out. It is a match that celebrates natural beauty with a bold twist.",
