        "numberTitle": "16. Auburn Copper Balayage Highlights",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_85_13.jpg",
        "description": "Auburn is the deeper, more mysterious cousin of bright copper, and when you combine the two through a balayage technique, the results are breathtaking. Auburn copper balayage weaves deep reddish-brown tones alongside bright copper ribbons for a look that feels rich and luxurious.\n\nThe auburn pieces anchor the color, giving it depth and sophistication, while the brighter copper strands add pops of vibrancy. This combination is especially stunning on thick, straight hair where the color can really shine and show off its full range. It is also one of the most low-maintenance options on this list since auburn naturally camouflages the grow-out phase. Your roots blend right in as the color softens over time.\n\nIt is elegant, bold, and endlessly versatile for any occasion or season.",
