        "numberTitle": "17. Chocolate Brown Copper Balayage",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_85_4.jpg",
        "description": "There is something undeniably luxurious about the pairing of rich chocolate brown with bright copper. This combination feels sophisticated, warm, and incredibly polished.\n\nThe technique involves sweeping bold copper highlights over a deep chocolate base, creating a contrast that is both striking and wearable. The chocolate tones keep the look grounded and elegant, while the copper streaks add movement and excitement. This color works beautifully on medium to thick hair textures. The darker base also means your roots will blend in naturally as the color grows out. Maintenance is surprisingly easy compared to all-over copper color. You only need touch-ups every few months to keep those bright pieces fresh.\n\nIt is a go-to option for anyone who wants warmth without going full redhead.",
