        "numberTitle": "1. Soft Red Balayage On Bob Haircut",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_91_17.jpg",
        "description": "A bob haircut with soft red balayage feels modern and fresh while still looking polished enough for everyday wear. Because bobs are shorter, your stylist usually keeps the balayage placement higher up, weaving subtle red and copper hues through the mid\u2011lengths so the color shows even when your hair is straight and sits above your shoulders.\n\nThis creates a dimensional finish that prevents the bob from appearing flat, especially on straight or slightly wavy textures where color variation does much of the work. You can tailor the intensity depending on your comfort, choosing barely\u2011there warmth or slightly more saturated red pieces that still blend seamlessly with your natural base.\n\nSince shorter hair gets trimmed more often, your ends stay healthier, which helps your subtle red balayage look shiny and crisp between glossing and toning appointments.",
