        "numberTitle": "2. Subtle Red Balayage With Shadow Root",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_91_19.jpg",
        "description": "Subtle red balayage with a shadow root combines low\u2011maintenance roots with soft, diffused color through the lengths. Your colorist intentionally keeps your root area deeper and slightly cooler, then blends into warmer red and copper tones starting a few inches down, which makes regrowth nearly invisible for weeks.\n\nThe shadow root also adds a modern, grown\u2011in feel that pairs well with both straight and wavy styling, especially on medium to long hair. Because the brightest tones sit away from the scalp, the overall effect stays subtle and there is less risk of clashing with your eyebrows or complexion near the hairline.\n\nMaintenance revolves around refreshing the mid\u2011lengths and ends with glosses or low\u2011volume balayage touch\u2011ups while leaving the root shadow mostly undisturbed, keeping both cost and time in the salon manageable.",
