        "numberTitle": "3. Subtle Red Balayage On Curly Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_91_8.jpg",
        "description": "Curly hair and subtle red balayage are a natural match, because hand\u2011painting lets your colorist place brightness exactly where your curls catch the light. On curls, the aim is to keep the roots and interior coils a bit deeper while adding fine, lighter red and copper strokes to the outer layers and ends, creating a three\u2011dimensional effect that emphasizes shape without sacrificing your depth.\n\nThe result is a halo of warm, red\u2011tinted curls that still look soft and natural when your hair is worn both defined and in a looser, fluffy finish. Since curls tend to be drier, your stylist should use gentle lightening and nourishing, bond\u2011protecting formulas during the balayage process to maintain elasticity and shine.\n\nAt home, lean on sulfate\u2011free cleansers, deep conditioners, and leave\u2011in products with UV protection so your subtle red tones don\u2019t fade quickly or look dull between salon visits.",
