        "numberTitle": "4. Warm Red Balayage On Shoulder Length Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_91_9.jpg",
        "description": "Shoulder length cuts give a balanced canvas for warm red balayage that is easy to style and maintain. Here, your colorist lifts select sections a little lighter than your base, then tones them with warm reds that mix copper and soft gold so the overall effect is a glowy, sunset\u2011like warmth instead of a single flat red.\n\nThis length is long enough to show a gradient from darker roots to lighter ends but short enough that damaged tips can be trimmed off regularly, keeping your hair healthy as you color. Styling with a simple blowout, round\u2011brush bend, or loose waves will highlight the warm ribbons and make your hair look fuller thanks to the added dimension.\n\nFor maintenance, space out lightening appointments and focus on frequent glosses plus at\u2011home masks that protect both the red tone and the integrity of your shoulder\u2011length cut.",
