        "numberTitle": "5. Rose Copper Balayage On Light Brown Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_91_10.jpg",
        "description": "Rose copper balayage on light brown hair brings a softer, slightly pink\u2011kissed twist to traditional copper red. The colorist first creates gentle balayage highlights a couple of levels lighter than your natural light brown, then tones them with a mix of copper and rose hues so the result looks warm but with a subtle rosy cast.\n\nThis combination is especially flattering on cool or neutral skin tones that might find pure copper too orange, because the rose note balances the warmth and adds a romantic feel. On hair, the color reads as multi\u2011dimensional rather than overtly pink, especially when styled in soft waves or smooth, glossy blowouts that show off different reflections in various lighting.\n\nKeep this shade looking fresh by avoiding over\u2011washing, using color\u2011depositing conditioners when needed, and scheduling regular glosses that refresh both the rose and copper elements without excessive lightening.",
