        "description": "Face framing red balayage highlights are ideal if you want a subtle change concentrated near your features rather than all over your head. Your stylist paints delicate red and copper pieces around the hairline, focusing on the sections that fall forward when you wear your hair down, so you see a halo of warmth while the rest of your hair stays closer to your natural shade.\n\nThis technique works beautifully with any length, from bobs to long hair, and is especially flattering when paired with curtain bangs or soft face\u2011framing layers that show off the color. Because the balayage is localized, appointments are faster and more budget\u2011friendly than full\u2011head transformations, yet the impact around your face is still noticeable in selfies and real life.\n\nProtecting this delicate area with UV filters, hats in strong sun, and color\u2011safe shampoo helps your red pieces stay vibrant and prevents the hairline from drying out.",
