        "image": "assets/doc_b_91_20.jpg",
        "description": "Low maintenance red balayage is perfect if you love the idea of red but do not have time for frequent salon visits. The strategy is to keep your natural base as the foundation, add soft balayage in red, copper, or auburn tones only where needed for brightness, and avoid high\u2011contrast placements that show a strong line as they grow out.\n\nYour stylist may recommend techniques like face framing pieces, mid\u2011length\u2011focused color, or subtle ends\u2011only balayage that can go months between full appointments, with quick gloss sessions in between to refresh tone. Choosing slightly deeper, more natural reds instead of very bright neon shades also helps, because these tones fade more gracefully and blend better with your base.\n\nAt home, protect your investment by washing less often, using cool water, and relying on color\u2011safe products so your subtle red balayage stays pretty and dimensional for as long as possible.",
