        "image": "assets/doc_b_91_4.jpg",
        "description": "For naturally blonde or lightened hair, a subtle strawberry red balayage brings in warmth while still reading as soft and light. Instead of going full copper or vibrant red, your colorist works with peachy, rose, and light strawberry tones, painting them over selected mid\u2011lengths and ends to create a whisper of red that blends into your existing blonde highlights.\n\nThe effect is especially flattering on fair to light\u2011medium skin tones because it adds a healthy flush around the face and makes blue or green eyes stand out without feeling too bold. Since the base is already light, minimal lifting is required, which helps keep hair healthier and reduces damage compared to darker transformations.\n\nAt home, treat this look like any pastel\u2011leaning color: wash with cool water, limit heat styling, and refresh the tone with a color\u2011depositing mask in soft strawberry or rose gold shades when it starts to fade.",
