        "image": "assets/doc_b_92_2.jpg",
        "description": "On straight hair, apricot copper balayage looks glossy and modern, because the color appears as smooth ribbons instead of diffused streaks. A stylist will often start with a medium copper root melt, then stretch soft apricot and copper blonde tones down the lengths using very fine, blended sections.\n\nThis creates a glass\u2011like finish that works especially well if you love blunt or lightly layered cuts that hit below the shoulders. If your natural hair is light brown or dark blonde, you may not need heavy lightening; your colorist can glaze in apricot copper tones for a softer lift.\n\nProtect your hair by applying a heat protectant and lightweight smoothing serum before flat\u2011ironing, which preserves shine and helps the copper reflections look polished instead of frizzy or dry.",
