        "description": "Keeping auburn balayage on dark hair looking fresh and vibrant requires a consistent, thoughtful care routine. Color-safe shampoo and conditioner are your best friends \u2014 regular sulfate-free products help protect both your dark base and your auburn tones from fading too quickly.\n\nA weekly deep conditioning treatment or hair mask is especially important if your balayage involved any lightening, as lifted strands tend to be more porous and need extra moisture. Using a color-depositing conditioner in a warm auburn or red shade can refresh your tones between salon visits and extend the life of your color significantly.\n\nProtecting your hair from heat is also crucial \u2014 always apply a heat protectant before blow-drying or styling. Refreshing your balayage every 12 to 16 weeks keeps the color looking intentional and vibrant.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Keeping auburn balayage on dark hair looking fresh and vibrant requires a consistent, thoughtful care routine. Color-safe shampoo and conditioner are your best friends \u2014 regular sulfate-free products help protect both your dark base and your auburn tones from fading too quickly.",
          "A weekly deep conditioning treatment or hair mask is especially important if your balayage involved any lightening, as lifted strands tend to be more porous and need extra moisture. Using a color-depositing conditioner in a warm auburn or red shade can refresh your tones between salon visits and extend the life of your color significantly.",
          "Protecting your hair from heat is also crucial \u2014 always apply a heat protectant before blow-drying or styling. Refreshing your balayage every 12 to 16 weeks keeps the color looking intentional and vibrant."
        ],
