        "numberTitle": "20. Butterscotch Auburn Balayage on Dark Hair",
        "image": "assets/doc_b_93_15.jpg",
        "description": "Butterscotch auburn balayage is a warm, golden-tinted take on the classic auburn look that feels rich, sweet, and incredibly flattering. It blends deep chestnut brown with a reddish base, then layers in caramel and copper balayage tones that give the overall look a golden warmth.\n\nThe butterscotch tones are slightly lighter and more golden than traditional auburn, which makes them particularly flattering on women with cool skin tones who might find straight auburn a little too warm or intense. The mix of reddish-brown and butterscotch-caramel creates a multi-tonal result that looks wonderfully dimensional and complex \u2014 especially when the hair is styled with loose waves that allow the different tones to catch the light from multiple angles.",
