            "description": "Medium length espresso brunette hair is a great choice if you want the drama of a dark, glossy shade without committing to extra-long maintenance. A cut that hits between the collarbone and just below the shoulders gives enough length for waves, curls, or sleek blowouts while still feeling easy to style every day. Ask for a rich espresso brunette base with soft, blended dimension\u2014think barely there lowlights or subtle, slightly lighter ribbons that sit only one to two levels above your base. This keeps the color from looking too solid while still reading as a deep brunette overall. Medium length hair also works well with face-framing pieces and long layers that add movement, which helps show off the glossy finish when the light hits. To keep your espresso shade vibrant, use heat protectant before hot tools and schedule gloss appointments every six to eight weeks.",
